hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"11023","(11023) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It begins after ablution. By washing the head."
"11024","(11024) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The dead are to be performed according to their ablution. For prayer, then wash with water, then wash with Sidr and water, then wash with water."
"11025","(11025) Abd al-Samad narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of a sheikh from the people of Kufa called Ziyad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: Camphor is placed on the places of prostration of the dead."
"11026","(11026) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I told Aisha: The dead person's head with a marshmallow? She said, “Do not be mean to your dead.”"
"11027","(11027) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If there is no Sidr, it will not harm you."
"11028","(11028) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: They do not wash it with two fresh palms while they are able Ali Al-Sidr"
"11029","(11029) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said, “I wash the dead person with a lot of Sidr.” There is sidr and marshmallow, and if it is not marshmallow, then with ashnan."
"11030","(11030) Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: If the distress of the dead is prolonged, it is washed away. With sorrows."
"11031","(11031) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: Do not wash me with Sidr."
"11032","(11032) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: If there is no Sidr So marshmallow."
"11033","(11033) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They mentioned about him washing the dead, so they said: like ablution. The man from impurity."
"11034","(11034) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Mu’tamir, on the authority of his followers, who said: The dead person is sufficient for washing what is sufficient for washing. The side"
"11035","(11035) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, who said: I came to Medina and asked about washing the dead. He said: Some of them said: Do to your dead woman as you would do to your bride, except that you do not create her."
"11036","(11036) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He used to say about the dead person when something came out of him after He washed it, he said, he washed what came out of it, he said, and Ibn Sirin used to say that the washing should be repeated."
"11037","(11037) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Sulayman al-Taymi, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: It should be washed twice."
"11038","(11038) Hushaym told us, on the authority of some of the Kufans, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, similar to what Al-Hasan said."
"11039","(11039) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I said to Hammad the dead man, when something came out of him after he had finished with him, he said: That place is washed."
"11040","(11040) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If anything comes out of it, water is poured over it, And his ablution did not cease."
"11041","(11041) Yazeed narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Yunus: In a dead person, something comes out of it after washing. He said: It will be repeated. He must wash twice, and if something comes out of him, he must wash again two to seven times, unless they fear that He relaxes and spoils them."
"11042","(11042) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The stomach of the dead person is squeezed gently in the first place. And the second"
"11043","(11043) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The stomach of the dead is squeezed on the first day. He washed it and squeezed it lightly."
"11044","(11044) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He squeezes his stomach gently."
"11045","(11045) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He came to us while we were washing a dead person, and he said: Tear it apart, and do not squeeze it, for you do not know what comes out in squeezing."
"11046","(11046) Ibn Mubarak and Abd al-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Ali was sought by someone The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was looking for a dead person and did not find it, so he said: May my father be blessed when he was alive and I was blessed when he was dead. (Abu Dawud) 415)"
"11047","(11047) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: Do not squeeze my stomach."
"11048","(11048) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said, “Disperse the dead, and do not bury it.”"
"11049","(11049) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, he said: He recommended Abdul Rahman bin Abi Bakr: If I die, shake me off, or shake me off."
"11050","(11050) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Do not move the head of the dead."
"11051","(11051) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: Do not make me sit."
"11052","(11052) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, that it was The dead are washed with bath."
"11053","(11053) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Water is boiled for the dead."
"11054","(11054) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, that he hated being taken from someone who was stubborn or unjust. After death, he used to say that the sick person’s family should do this while he is heavy."
"11055","(11055) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: trimming the nails of the dead, he said Shu`ba: So I mentioned that to Hammad, but he denied it and said: What do you think, if he was uncircumcised, should he be circumcised?"
"11056","(11056) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, that Sa’d washed a dead person and called for Moses. So he shaved it."
"11057","(11057) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, that it was astonishing for him, when a sick person became heavy, that It will be taken from his mustache, nails, and pubic hair. If he dies, nothing will be taken from him."
"11058","(11058) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, that whenever he saw something obscene from the dead, Of poetry and nails he took and penned."
"11059","(11059) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Uqba bin Abi Al-Saba’i, he said: Abu Al-Aliyah Al-Qaisi narrated to us, Abu Al-Malih Al-Hudhali advised them, saying: When he dies, they should take some of his hair and nails."
"11060","(11060) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, that Sa’d washed a dead person and called with a razor. So he shaved it."
"11061","(11061) Abdul-Rahman bin Mahdi and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Abi When Layla is dead, some of his hair and nails will fall out. He said, “It will be with him.”"
"11062","(11062) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin and the daughters of Sirin, they said: What is buried with the dead? Hair or other hair falling out."
"11063","(11063) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, who said: I heard Al-Hasan say that he trims the nails of the dead person and his mustache if it grows long. He said: I told Al-Hasan, “It should be put with him.” He said, “Yes.”"
"11064","(11064) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalababi, he said: He liked to He will be made with him."
"11065","(11065) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, That Qais bin Saad passed by a man whose finger had fallen off, so she was buried with him."
"11066","(11066) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’i, on the authority of Hafsa, that she said: “Mind the dead person’s hair, for it makes With him"
"11067","(11067) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: There is no harm in a menstruating woman or a woman in a state of sexual impurity washing the dead."
"11068","(11068) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin that they used to hate being washed. The one who is in a state of sexual impurity and the dead menstruating woman."
"11069","(11069) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: My mother was sent to Alqamah. You ask him about a menstruating woman washing a dead person but he did not see any harm in it."
"11070","(11070) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If the woman dies in Men, there is not with them a woman upon whom water was poured from over the clothes in the morning."
"11071","(11071) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: I said to Safiyya bint Abi Ubaid: The woman is dying. With the men, but there is no woman with them. She said: They will bury her in her clothes."
"11072","(11072) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’; In a woman who dies with the men, he said: Do tayammum, then she is buried in her clothes, and the man is like that."
"11073","(11073) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that he said: If The woman died with the men, and there was no woman with her. He said: They should lead her on dry ablutions, but they should not wash her. And when the man dies With women, so too."
"11074","(11074) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, who said: He performed tayammum on the earth and the man likewise."
"11075","(11075) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, on the authority of Abi Salamah; Concerning a man who dies with the women, he said: His wife will wash him, but if his wife is not there, then he should perform dry ablution in the desert, and the woman will die. With men, there is no woman with them. He said: Her husband should wash her, and if not, then by women from the wives of the People of the Book. They pour water for them and We wash them."
"11076","(11076) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; “In a woman, she dies with the men.” He said, “They pour water over her, then they bury her.” And in a man, he dies with the women. They pour water on him, then bury him."
"11077","(11077) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that in a woman she dies with Men, he said, a thermos in water."
"11078","(11078) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, that Aba Bakr instructed Asma, his two sons, Umays, to wash him."
"11079","(11079) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, that Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq when At his death, he instructed Asma’ bint Umays to bathe her as she was fasting, so he appointed for her to break her fast."
"11080","(11080) Waki’ ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Salih al-Dhan, or Hayyan al-Araj, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd. He commanded that his wife wash him."
"11081","(11081) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Bishr bin Abdullah bin Yassar, who said: I heard Suleiman bin Musa say: You wash him."
"11082","(11082) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: He washes every One of them is his friend."
"11083","(11083) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, on the authority of Abi Salamah; Concerning a man who dies with the women, he said: His wife should wash him."
"11084","(11084) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A woman should wash her husband."
"11085","(11085) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Abu Musa washed him His wife"
"11086","(11086) Muammar bin Sulaiman Al-Raqqi narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Dawud bin Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The man has more right to wash his wife."
"11087","(11087) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not see any harm in doing that. A man and his wife."
"11088","(11088) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad said: My wife’s mother or sister refused to You wash her, so I took over to wash her myself."
"11089","(11089) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of al-Hasan. They said: He washes Each one of them has its own companion."
"11090","(11090) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, on the authority of My father greeted her in the mirror. She would die with the men. There was no woman with them. He said, “Her husband will wash her.”"
"11091","(11091) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a woman dies, her marriage between her and her is cut off. Her husband"
"11092","(11092) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: A man should not wash his wife. And this is the opinion of Sufyan."
"11093","(11093) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Bishr bin Abdullah bin Yassar, he said: He said: I heard Suleiman bin Musa. He says: A man washes his wife."
"11094","(11094) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Masruq, who said she died A woman to Omar, and he said: I was more worthy of her when she was alive, but now you are more worthy of her."
"11095","(11095) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, he said: I was in a gathering in which Qasamah bin Zuhair and some sheikhs were present. They caught up with Omar bin Al-Khattab, and he said: A man who had been married to a woman from the Banu Amir bin Sa’sa’a, and he used to praise her. Well, when the time of the sweeping plague came, she was stabbed, and when she became heavy, she said, “I am a strange woman, so there is no one to help me but you.” So she died. So I washed her, and I took care of her. Awf said, “I did not see any of those old men blaming him, nor did he find fault with him.”"
"11096","(11096) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, that Abu Qalababi washed his daughter."
"11097","(11097) Shababā told us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Abu Al-Hasan Al-Wasiti, who said: Abu Qalābā washed his daughter, so I told him What makes you know? He said: We were in his house and he came out to us and told us that he had done that. He said: She was a young slave."
"11098","(11098) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not see any harm in a woman washing a boy if He was weaned, and there was something beyond him."
"11099","(11099) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, Muhammad was asked about a woman washing a boy, and he said: I do not know of any harm in it."
"11100","(11100) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The boy who has sought to be shrouded should be placed in rags to be washed. Women"
"11101","(11101) Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: Hafsa bint Sirin narrated to me, that Umm Atiyya said: It is combed into three horns, meaning the son of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"11102","(11102) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He used to say, “When a woman washes, her hair will dissolve.” Three thaibs, then their successors were appointed."
"11103","(11103) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Muthanna bin Bilal Al-Abdi, he said: Our sheikhs who They witnessed Zayd ibn Suhan when he was injured on the day of the camel. He said, “Tighten my clothes and do not wash away any blood or dirt from me. A quarrelsome man."
"11104","(11104) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: When he was asked about the martyr’s washing, he said: On the hadith of Hujr ibn Adiy, he said: Hujr ibn Adiyy said to those of his family who were present with him: Do not wash off his blood, and do not divorce him. Protect me and bury me in my clothes, for I and Muawiyah will meet on the avenue tomorrow."
"11105","(11105) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that a man from Abdullah’s companions was killed by the enemy, so we buried him in his clothes."
"11106","(11106) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: Saad bin Ubaid Al-Qari said on the Day of Al-Qadisiyah, “Indeed, we will meet the enemy tomorrow, God willing, and we will be guided, so do not wash away our blood, nor We will be shrouded except in a garment that is on us."
"11107","(11107) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Makhoul bin Rashid Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Al-Izar bin Harith. Al-Abdi, he said: Zaid bin Suhan said on the Day of the Camel: Throw me into the ground as a sand, and do not wash away the blood from me, and do not remove it from me. Clothes, except for the socks, for I perform Hajj. I perform Hajj."
"11108","(11108) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar and Sufyan, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Al-Muthanna, Sufyan said, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Zaid Ibn Suhan, and Mas’ar said, on the authority of Mus’ab Ibn Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Zayd Ibn Suhan, that he said on the Day of the Camel, “Bury us,” and the dust did not fall. From our blood."
"11109","(11109) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan that they said: The martyr is washed unless he dies, except a non-mahram person."
"11110","(11110) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zakaria narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, that Hanzala ibn al-Rahib was purified by the angels."
"11111","(11111) Waki’ told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbas, on the authority of Ammar, he said: Bury me in my clothes, for I am quarreling."
"11112","(11112) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: I heard Yahya bin Abbas speaking about Qais bin Abi Hazim, on the authority of Ammar, similar to him."
"11113","(11113) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When the dead person is raised, he is buried in his clothes, even if It was raised, and with it a noun was done with it that cannot be done with anything else."
"11114","(11114) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Uzza, on the authority of Amir, about a man killed by thieves, He said: He should be buried in his clothes and not washed."
"11115","(11115) Abu Asama told us, Thabit bin Amara told us, he said: I heard Ghanim bin Qays say: It is said that the martyr will be buried. In his clothes, and he should not be washed."
"11116","(11116) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the case of a murdered person, if he had a period of mourning, he should be washed."
"11117","(11117) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he died in battle He was buried and his socks or sandals were removed, and when he was taken up with his eyelids on, then he died, what is done to a dead person is done to him."
"11118","(11118) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave orders to Hamza when He was martyred and washed. (Hakim 195)"
"11119","(11119) Shababih told us, saying: Laith bin Saad informed us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b bin Malik, that Jabir bin Abdullah informed him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray for the killing of anyone, nor did he They are washed. (Bukhari 1343. Abu Dawud 3130)"
"11120","(11120) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said, Umar was shrouded and embalmed. And he washed him."
"11121","(11121) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, in the same way, except that he said: He was one of The best martyrs."
"11122","(11122) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he is killed in He was buried in his clothes and was not washed."
"11123","(11123) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Marthad, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, he said when Ali was stoned His commentators, Hamdan, came to Ali and they said: What should be done with her? He said: Do to her as you do to your women when they die. Butane"
"11124","(11124) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father He said: When a goat was stoned, they said: O Messenger of God, what shall we do with it? He said: Do to it what you do to your dead, of washing and shrouding. And the spices and may the blessings and peace of God be upon him."
"11125","(11125) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A drowning person is washed, shrouded, embalmed, and whatever is done to him. It is made by something else."
"11126","(11126) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a man in a state of impurity or a menstruating woman dies, something will be done to them. It is made with other than them."
"11127","(11127) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: When a person in a state of ritual impurity dies, he said, “He should be washed due to his impurity, and he should be washed.” Bathing the dead person, and the same applies to a menstruating woman if she purifies herself, then dies before washing."
"11128","(11128) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Hakim bin Jabir, who said: When Ibn Qays died, he said Al-Hasan bin Ali: If you have washed it, do not perform it until you call me to prayer. Then he came and he performed ablution with spices as a ritual ablution."
"11129","(11129) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Bakr, who said: I heard Salim and Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah say, It was mentioned to them that the perfume of the dead person was mentioned. They said: Leave it between him and his clothes."
"11130","(11130) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said, “His clothes and spices should be piled up on Mosques"
"11131","(11131) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, regarding the embalming of the dead. He said, “It begins with In his mosques"
"11132","(11132) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When he has finished washing, his mosques will be followed. With perfume"
"11133","(11133) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warath narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of a sheikh from the people of Kufa, called Ziyad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, said: Camphor is placed on the place where the dead person prostrates."
"11134","(11134) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: After he had finished washing the dead, Ayoub would apply He covered his face with his cotton, but Muhammad did not do that."
"11135","(11135) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of al-Hasan, that he was of the opinion that hardships are sufficient if they do not There shall be cotton for the dead woman."
"11136","(11136) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said, “Should I stuff the celery?” He said, “Yes.” I said, “so that nothing comes out of it.” He said, “Yes.”"
"11137","(11137) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He is resurrected from the dead when they fear that he will come out. From him"
"11138","(11138) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He stuffed his back, ears, and nose."
"11139","(11139) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, he said: I heard Ibn Sirin say: The anus of the dead is stuffed and he dies. And his nostrils were covered with cotton, and Muhammad said, “I cannot cure his anus,” so treat it with his tongue."
"11140","(11140) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Umayyah al-Azdi, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: When May the dead person block his eyes and ears with hardship."
"11141","(11141) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, that he put in his spices a sachet of musk, or It contains a poem of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"11142","(11142) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Ibn Umar was asked about musk. Regarding spices, he said: Isn’t it one of the best of your perfumes?"
"11143","(11143) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, who said: Ibn Umar was asked if the dead are closest. Musk, he said, is it not one of the best of your perfumes?"
"11144","(11144) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna bin Saeed, on the authority of his followers, he said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab Concerning musk in the spices of the dead, he said: There is no problem with it. Jabir bin Zayd was asked about that, and he said: There is no problem with it."
"11145","(11145) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, that he was asked about the perfumes of the dead. With musk. He said, Yes. Do they not put musk in that which they stone the stones with?"
"11146","(11146) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Harun bin Saad, that Ali recommended that he be placed in Spicy perfume is a musk, and he said it is the best spices of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"11147","(11147) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib and Muhammad bin Suqi, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said when Salman invaded Balanjar, a bundle of musk fell on his stomach, and when he returned, he entrusted it to his wife, and when he fell ill, he died. As he was dying, he said to his wife: Show me the bag that I entrusted to you. So she brought it to him, and he said: Bring me a clean vessel. So she brought it, and he said: Add it, then sacrifice it around me, for it is a creation of God’s creation that they will not eat. Food, and they smelled the smell, and he said: Get out of me and treat me. She said: So I left, then I came back and he had finished."
"11148","(11148) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar embalmed a dead person with musk."
"11149","(11149) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibn Mughaffal, who said: Omar said, “Do not embalm me with musk.”"
"11150","(11150) Hatem bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar bin Muhammad, on the authority of Sufyan bin Asim, who said: I witnessed Omar bin Abdul Aziz. He said to his mother, “I see you softening my wheat, so do not put any musk in it.”"
"11151","(11151) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, that he said: There is no harm in amber in spices, and he said : It is only gum and he hates musk for the living and the dead, and he said it is dead."
"11152","(11152) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he disliked musk for the dead."
"11153","(11153) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked musk for the living and the dead. And he says, “The Muslims hated him and said, ‘He is dead.’”"
"11154","(11154) Yahya bin Al-Yaman and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawad, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, that he disliked touch in Spices"
"11155","(11155) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He was shrouded in three Yemeni garments, without a shirt or turban. So we said to Aisha: They claim that he was shrouded in an ink’s sack, so she said, “They brought a ink’s sack, but they did not shroud him in it.” (Abu Dawud 3144, Bukhari 1273)"
"11156","(11156) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was shrouded. May God bless him and grant him peace, in three garments: the shirt in which he died, and a Najran garment."
"11157","(11157) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I passed by one of the gatherings of Banu Abdul Muttalib and asked them about How the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was shrouded, and they said: In three garments, neither a shirt, nor a cloak, nor turban"
"11158","(11158) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was shrouded in Two desert garments and an ink cloak. He said: My father advised me to do that."
"11159","(11159) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was shrouded in a red garment and a garment. torn"
"11160","(11160) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said, when Abu Bakr came, he said In how many garments was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, shrouded? I said, in three shroud garments? He said, “So he looked at a garment that he was wearing, and he said: Wash this and add two more garments to it.” I said, “Rather, we will buy it for you.” He wore new clothes, and said: The living is more deserving of new clothes than the dead, but it is for the dead."
"11161","(11161) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Abu Bakr. How did you shroud the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? I said, “In three garments.” He said, “So wash my garment.” And they bought me a dress from the market. She said, “We are well-off.” He said, “O my children, the living is more deserving of a new one than the dead. For the sake of Allah and the pus."
"11162","(11162) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, who said: Abu A virgin wearing two Sahelian garments and a robe with a woven robe, with which he was commanded to be washed."
"11163","(11163) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that Umar was shrouded in three garments."
"11164","(11164) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, who said: Omar said: A man should be shrouded in three garments, not Transgress. Indeed, God does not like transgressors."
"11165","(11165) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Al-Jaadi, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, he said: Abu Hurairah said They shrouded me in three garments and wrapped me in wrapping."
"11166","(11166) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Haram, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked, Concerning the deceased, how much of the shroud is enough for him? He said: Ibn Abbas used to say one garment, or three garments, or five. dresses"
"11167","(11167) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, on the authority of Abu Tufayl, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said They shrouded me in these two garments, in the two garments in which they were created."
"11168","(11168) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdul God Ibn Amr said: The dead person is shrouded in three garments: a shirt, a loincloth, and a wrap."
"11169","(11169) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Nafi’; Waqid bin Abdullah died, and Ibn Omar shrouded him in five garments: a shirt, a loincloth, three scrolls, and his turban."
"11170","(11170) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, who said: Hamza was shrouded in a garment."
"11171","(11171) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He shrouded Hamza in a garment, that garment was a tiger. (Tirmidhi 997. Ahmad 3/329)"
"11172","(11172) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that Safiyya went on the Day of Uhud wearing two garments. You want to shroud Hamza bin Abdul Muttalib in them? He said, “One of the two garments is wider than the other.” He said, “And it was found on its side.” A man from the Ansar, so she cast lots between them and wrapped the one in the wider garment, the one with the wider garment, and the other in the remaining garment."
"11173","(11173) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Suwayd, that Abu Bakr was shrouded in two garments."
"11174","(11174) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Suwayd, who said: The man and the woman are shrouded in Two dresses"
"11175","(11175) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of Ghanim ibn Qays, who said: We used to be shrouded in two garments. And the three and four."
"11176","(11176) Ibn Hubab narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Salih narrated to me, saying: Yazid bin Zaid, the client of Abu Usayd, narrated to me. On the authority of Abu Asid, he said, “We are with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at the grave of Hamza, so the tiger stretched out over his head.” Then his legs were uncovered, so he extended his legs and his head was uncovered, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Place them on him. His head, and put upon his feet of the tree of the Haramel tree. (Bukhari 3224, Ibn Saad 15)"
"11177","(11177) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Umayyah, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: The dead person should not be circulated."
"11178","(11178) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Khabab bin Al-Art, who said, “We emigrated with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” May God bless him and grant him peace. In the path of God, we seek the face of God Almighty, so our reward is obligatory upon God. For there are those of us who have passed away who have not eaten from The reward for one of them was Mus’ab bin Umair. He was killed on the day of Uhud, and we did not find anything for him to be shrouded in except a tiger, so we were When We place it on his head, his legs come out. When We place it on his feet, his head comes out. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. May God bless him and grant him peace: Place some of what is on his head, and place on his feet of greenery, and among us is he whose fruit is abundant, so he is He guides her. \n(Bukhari 1276 and Abu Dawud 2868)"
"11179","(11179) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of his father, that He recommended that he be shrouded in three garments in which he would be placed in a row."
"11180","(11180) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A man is shrouded in three garments. And the garment and the wrapper."
"11181","(11181) Yahya bin Al-Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The dead person should not be circulated."
"11182","(11182) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The dead person is shrouded in two garments."
"11183","(11183) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he liked to shroud the dead. In a shirt with a button and two sleeves like a snake."
"11184","(11184) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was shrouded. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, in three garments, one of which is a silk scarf. (Ibn Saad 284)"
"11185","(11185) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Aisha; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was wrapped in an inky blanket, so that was true to him, according to what Ali bin Hussein said. (Bukhari 5814, Muslim 48)"
"11186","(11186) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was shrouded. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, in three garments, one of which is a cloak."
"11187","(11187) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said that more than one of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He was shrouded in one garment."
"11188","(11188) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that Hamza bin Abd al-Muttalib was shrouded in one garment."
"11189","(11189) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Aisha, that Abu Bakr said: If I die, wash me with two sheets and shroud me in them, for the living is more in need of something new than the dead."
"11190","(11190) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Umar, on the authority of Aisha said: The dead should not be shrouded in less than three garments for those who estimate."
"11191","(11191) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, that Hamzah was shrouded in a garment."
"11192","(11192) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Khaythami, on the authority of Suwayd, he said: Do not shroud me except in two garments."
"11193","(11193) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Iyas bin Daghfal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Qais bin Abbad, on the authority of his father, that He commanded that they shroud me in a velvet robe and cover my bed like the white robe in which I used to pray."
"11194","(11194) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas was shrouded in five garments."
"11195","(11195) Suwayd bin Amr narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Ibn The Hanafi, on the authority of Ali, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was shrouded in seven garments. (Ahmad 1/102)"
"11196","(11196) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Muhammad, that he used to say that a woman who has menstruated should be shrouded in five days. Two dresses, or three."
"11197","(11197) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Izza, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said, “Be shrouded” A woman wears five garments: a breastplate, a veil, a wrap, a girdle, and a piece of rag that is on her stomach."
"11198","(11198) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A woman should be shrouded in five garments of armor and a veil. And a belt and two wrappers."
"11199","(11199) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Omar, who said: A woman should be shrouded in five garments."
"11200","(11200) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The woman should be shrouded in five garments. The belt, and the armor, and the veil, and the wrapping and the rags that are tied around it."
"11201","(11201) Abd al-Rahman bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The woman should be shrouded in five garments. In the armor, the veil, the robe, the garment, and the rags."
"11202","(11202) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Suwayd, who said: The woman and the man are shrouded in Two dresses"
"11203","(11203) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The woman should be shrouded in a shield and a veil. And a wrap, and a garment, and rags."
"11204","(11204) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The rag is placed on her stomach and wrapped around it. Her thighs"
"11205","(11205) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, regarding the fifth piece of clothing that was wrapped around the thighs under the The shield"
"11206","(11206) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Ezza, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: And a rag is on Her stomach"
"11207","(11207) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The rag is pulled over the garment."
"11208","(11208) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The boy should be shrouded in a rag."
"11209","(11209) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: The weaned and the infant shall be shrouded in a cloth. In addition to that, he was shrouded in a shirt and two rags."
"11210","(11210) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, about the fall. He said, “If he wishes, he can be shrouded for three days.” dresses"
"11211","(11211) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He shrouds whatever is possible."
"11212","(11212) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The boy should be shrouded in a rag, even if he has He sought"
"11213","(11213) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Amr, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A miscarriage is shrouded in rags"
"11214","(11214) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The boy should be shrouded in a garment."
"11215","(11215) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The boy is shrouded in a veil and made It includes a shirt and a wrap."
"11216","(11216) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman, who said: I asked Al-Hasan about a slave girl: If she dies, does she get drunk and does not menstruate? He said: No, but you will be shrouded in three garments."
"11217","(11217) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: Anas ibn Sirin’s son died and she squeezed it, so Ibn Sirin ordered them to They will wrap her in wine and two wrappers."
"11218","(11218) Ubaidullah bin Musa told us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a slave girl who has not reached puberty, he said, she should be shrouded in one garment."
"11219","(11219) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: I asked Umm Abd al-Hamid ibn Sirin if she had seen Hafsiah, when she was washed, how would she do it with the woman’s veil? She said, “Yes.” She used to cover it as a snake is cleansed, then she would remove from the veil. The length of a cubit, and you spread it over her backside, then cover that leftover space and cover her face with it."
"11220","(11220) Affan told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his followers, he said: Al-Hasan used to say that when a dead person dies, the turban should be placed in the middle. His head, then his two ends are aligned like this to his body. He said: Ibn Sirin said: It is circulated as it is circulated. The living"
"11221","(11221) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He wears it."
"11222","(11222) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The clothes of the dead are piled up on a pall, or Reeds, he said, and Muhammad was of the opinion that if they did that, then it was good, and I would love for him to be embellished with stones on him after he had put on his clothes. So it keeps its scent."
"11223","(11223) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Hafs, who said: Do not burn the dead except his clothes."
"11224","(11224) Abd bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asmaa, that she said when she died: I died, so wash me, shroud me, and gather my clothes."
"11225","(11225) Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: His clothes should be reddened three times."
"11226","(11226) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaidullah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: His garment is tied with a string."
"11227","(11227) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin that they used to burn the clothes of the dead. A string"
"11228","(11228) Abu Muawiyah and Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’biy, who said: The clothes of the dead are gathered together, except Ibn Mushar said: Whatever you want."
"11229","(11229) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The dead person is buried with a string of embers."
"11230","(11230) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah’s companions used to say: He washed him once and gathered up his clothes."
"11231","(11231) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurri, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said, burying the dead is a Witr prayer."
"11232","(11232) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Qutbi bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When you throw burying stones for the dead, throw them three stones over him.” (Ahmad 331) Abu Ali 2300)"
"11233","(11233) Sahl bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, that Muhammad used to admire the pure shroud."
"11234","(11234) Abu Hayyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of Maimun, who said: They used to prefer that the woman be shrouded in a heavy The clothes"
"11235","(11235) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan and Muhammad, that it was astonishing that they were The shroud is linen."
"11236","(11236) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, bestowed upon you white clothes, so that your living may wear them and be shrouded in them. Your dead (Nasa’i 9643; Abd al-Razzaq 6298)"
"11237","(11237) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Maimun ibn Abi Shabib, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Wear white clothes and shroud your dead in them.\n(Tirmidhi 2810, Hakim 354)"
"11238","(11238) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The best of your clothes is white. (Abu Dawud 3874. Ahmad 1/247)"
"11239","(11239) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad that they said: There is no harm in a man being shrouded in a garment. Al-Harawi"
"11240","(11240) Shababi bin Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Huwayrith, that A woman, a bride, entered upon her husband wearing saffron clothes, and she died when she entered upon her. Aisha was asked, and she said: Bury her in the clothes she was wearing."
"11241","(11241) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: If one of you dies Let him shroud him well, he said: If he does not find anything, let him shroud him in an ink robe. (Muslim 49. Ahmad 3/329)"
"11242","(11242) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Umays, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Thabit, on the authority of Khathim ibn Amr, that Abd God bin Masoud commanded that he be shrouded in a garment whose price is the eighth of two hundred dirhams."
"11243","(11243) Bishr bin Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Alqamiya, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He loved beautiful shrouds. It is said that they visit one another over their shrouds."
"11244","(11244) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Sa’id ibn Hani narrated to us, on the authority of Umair. Ibn Al-Aswad Al-Sakouni, that Muadh Ibn Jabal left a will for his wife and went out, and she died, and We shrouded her in clothes that had good morals, so he came and... We raised our hands from her grave at that time, and he said: “Why have you shrouded her?” We said, “In her clothes are creations.” So we exhumed her and shrouded her. In new clothes, and he said, “Make good care of the shrouds of your dead, for they will be gathered in them.”"
"11245","(11245) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Bashir, on the authority of Abi Ya’li, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafi, who said: The dead have something from the shroud, but it is to honor the living."
"11246","(11246) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Do not defile your dead, for The believer is neither impure whether alive or dead."
"11247","(11247) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I told Ibn Umar: “I wash myself with Washing the dead, he said: No."
"11248","(11248) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Do not defile yourself. Your dead person does not have to be washed."
"11249","(11249) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I washed My mother was dead, so she said to me: “Ask, should I wash?” So I came to Ibn Umar and asked him, and he said: “Is it impure that I washed?” Then I came to Ibn Abbas and asked him, and he said something like that, was the unclean thing washed?"
"11250","(11250) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah was asked about the ritual ablution for washing the dead. He said: If your companion is impure, then wash with him."
"11251","(11251) Yahya bin Sa’id al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Aisha bint Sa’d, who said: Sa’d was given the call for his funeral. Saeed bin Zaid, while he was in Al-Baqi’, he came and washed him, shrouded him and embalmed him, then he came to his house and prayed over him, then He called for water and took a bath, then he said: I did not take a bath from his washing, and if it had been impure I would not have washed him, but I took a bath from the heat."
"11252","(11252) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas and Ibn Omar, who said: The one who washes the dead does not have to do so. Washed"
"11253","(11253) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Yazid al-Rashik, on the authority of Muadh, on the authority of Aisha, that she was asked about Who washes the deceased? She said: No."
"11254","(11254) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Al-Shahid, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, he said: Alqamah bin Abdullah Al-Muzani said: Four of the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, washed your father, but they did not suffice. They took off their sleeves and put their shirts into their pockets, and when they finished washing them, they performed their ablution for prayer."
"11255","(11255) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, he said: Khuza’i bin Ziyad narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, He said: Abdullah bin Mughaffal advised that Ibn Ziyad should not attend him, and that my companions should please me, so they sent for Aidh bin Amr. And Abu Barzah and some of his companions refused. They did more than tie their sleeves and put what was left of their shirts in their custody. When When they finished they did not do anything more than ablution."
"11256","(11256) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, that Ibn Umar shrouded a dead body and embalmed it, and did not He touches water."
"11257","(11257) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to say, “If your friend is impure, then take a bath.” From him"
"11258","(11258) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: If your friend is impure, take a bath. From him"
"11259","(11259) Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Musab bin Shaybi, on the authority of Talq bin Habib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubair, that Aisha narrated to him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He should wash after washing The dead"
"11260","(11260) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: A man asked Hudhayfy what I should do. He said: Wash him many times and then when you have finished, take a bath."
"11261","(11261) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Whoever washes a dead person Let him wash."
"11262","(11262) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said, from the Sunnah, whoever washes He was dead and washed."
"11263","(11263) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that two men from Ali’s companions and Abdullah’s companions bathed a dead person, and he did so. The one from Ali’s companions, and the one from Abdullah’s companions performed ablution."
"11264","(11264) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that He used to say: Whoever washes a dead body, let him wash himself, and whoever carries him, let him perform ablution."
"11265","(11265) Shababih told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Salih the client of the twins, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever washes a dead body, let him wash himself, and whoever carries him, let him perform ablution. (Ahmad 433, Bayhaqi 303)"
"11266","(11266) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, that when he washed a dead person, he would wash himself."
"11267","(11267) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Najiya bin Ka`b, on the authority of Ali, who said when he died Abu Talib: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said, O Messenger of God, your uncle, the misguided old man, has died. He said: So he said: Go. So he hid him, then do not say anything until you come to me. He said, “I hid him, then I came to him, so he commanded me, so I washed.” Then he called. I have supplications that please me, I have nothing that pleases me on earth. (Abu Dawud 3206; Ahmad 1/103)"
"11268","(11268) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal, who said: Whoever washes a dead person, then performs the ritual prayer. In him are trusts, he is free from his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him."
"11269","(11269) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asmaa, that she recommended that they not make Enough of wheat."
"11270","(11270) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he threw spices on the coffin."
"11271","(11271) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I saw offspring at the funeral of Al-Harith."
"11272","(11272) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, on the authority of Umar ibn Abdul Aziz, that he hated the offspring for The casket"
"11273","(11273) Hushaym bin Bashir narrated to us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin that they wanted to make Embalm on the coffin."
"11274","(11274) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of a companion of his, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, the same."
"11275","(11275) Yahya bin Sulaym al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, that he hated offspring. Which is placed on top of the coffin and it is said: “He will be blown into life and he will be blown into death”!"
"11276","(11276) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that Asma bint Umays was the first to bring the coffin."
"11277","(11277) Abdul Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, that Umm Ayman ordered the coffin for the women."
"11278","(11278) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, who said: They passed by Abu Majliz with a large coffin, and he said: It was raised. The Jews and Christians disagreed with them."
"11279","(11279) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the funeral of a woman was a woman, they would refrain. The bed, so they covered it with its supports, and behold, a man was placed on the stomach of the bed."
"11280","(11280) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of al-Rabi`, on the authority of al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin that they disliked that embers be burned on the bed of the dead."
"11281","(11281) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibn Mufaddal, who said: Omar said, “Do not follow me with a censer.”"
"11282","(11282) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, who said: Abu Hurairah said: No. You follow me with fire."
"11283","(11283) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Mujma’, on the authority of his paternal aunt Umm al-Nu’man bint Mujma’, on the authority of his son Abi Saeed, that Abu Saeed said: Do not follow me into hellfire, and do not place Christian velvet on my bed."
"11284","(11284) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Harun bin Abi Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umayr, on the authority of Aisha, Indeed, I have commanded that you do not follow me over a hot coal, and do not place red velvet on me."
"11285","(11285) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Ashhab, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, that he commanded not Do you follow me with noise or fire, and do not throw stones at me, meaning the path that is on the brink of the grave?"
"11286","(11286) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, that he saw a censer in He broke his funeral and said, “I heard Ibn Abbas saying, ‘Do not resemble the People of the Book.’”"
"11287","(11287) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin that they disliked that the funeral be followed. With a censer."
"11288","(11288) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If you bring it out, do not follow it with fire."
"11289","(11289) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated to be followed by a censer."
"11290","(11290) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: We visited Ibrahim al-Nakha’i in the morning, and they informed us that he had died and someone was buried. Night, he said, so Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad informed us that he commanded that you not follow his funeral with fire, and that you do not place on him anything Arzami laban, which is made from kannasat."
"11291","(11291) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: We came to Abraham’s house after his death and said anything. Did he recommend? They said: I command that he shall not be followed by fire, and adhere to my punishment, and do not put in my grave any brick of Arzmi."
"11292","(11292) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The funeral procession should not be followed by sound, fire, or people walking in front of it. (Abu Dawud 3163. Ahmad 2/528)"
"11293","(11293) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Hanash ibn al-Mu’tamir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He said the salutation at his funeral and saw a woman with a censer, so he said: Expel her. He continued standing until they said: O Messenger of God, she has disappeared. In the times of Medina."
"11294","(11294) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahak, who said: I saw Ibn Umar in His funeral, placing the bed on its shoulders between the two pillars."
"11295","(11295) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Salim bin Abdullah between my pillars. His mother's bed until he took her out of the house, along with Hamza and Ubaidullah. One of them took the right side of the bed and the other With ease."
"11296","(11296) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Marouf, a client of Quraysh, who said: I saw Al-Muttalib bin Abdullah bin Hantab. Between the two pillars was the bed of his son Al-Harith."
"11297","(11297) Waki’ and Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sa’d bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Sa’d At the foot of Abd al-Rahman bin Awf’s bed, he said: We brought him."
"11298","(11298) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I saw Abu Juhayfi at Abu Misra’s funeral. Taking the bedpost, he began to say, “May God forgive you, O Abu Misra.”"
"11299","(11299) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He hated to be among the rulers. A man carries the bed."
"11300","(11300) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Furat ibn Salman, who said: A funeral was taken from the house of Banu Dhu al-Khimar. He said: A young man among them placed the bed on his shoulders, and Maimoon took him by the hand and took him out."
"11301","(11301) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: I saw Abu Juhaif at the funeral of Abu Misra. And the burden is on his shoulders, and he says: O God, forgive Abu Misra."
"11302","(11302) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he hated to stand at the front of the bed or the back."
"11303","(11303) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He disliked it for a man to follow the funeral procession. He says: Ask forgiveness for him, may God forgive you."
"11304","(11304) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair bin Atiq, who said: I was at a funeral in which Sa’id bin Jubair, and a man said: Ask forgiveness for him, may God forgive you. Sa`id bin Jubair said: May God not forgive you."
"11305","(11305) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I was with him at his funeral. So he heard a man saying, “Ask forgiveness for him, may God forgive you, and he forbids you.”"
"11306","(11306) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, that he hated to say, “Ask forgiveness for him, he will be forgiven.” May God bless you"
"11307","(11307) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: The first thing I heard at his funeral was: Ask forgiveness For him at the funeral of Saad bin Aws."
"11308","(11308) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked that He says:"
"11309","(11309) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked to say: Ask forgiveness, may God forgive you."
"11310","(11310) Abu Muti’ told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, that he was at a funeral and heard a man say, and he said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab: What does this person of yours say?!"
"11311","(11311) Qubaisa narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ ibn Abi Rashid, that Sa’id ibn Jubayr heard a man saying in Funeral: Ask forgiveness for him, may God forgive you, so he became angry."
"11312","(11312) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaab, who said: We were at a funeral and some people rose from the grave. The retaliators make their voices heard, and Abu Qalaba said, “They used to venerate the dead with the knife.”"
"11313","(11313) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, who said: It was The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, recommended lowering the voice three times: when fighting, when reciting the Qur’an, and at funerals."
"11314","(11314) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Qays ibn Abbad, who said: They were the companions of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he mentioned something similar to it. (Abu Dawud 2449. Hakim 116)"
"11315","(11315) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was At his funeral, he was mostly silent and talked to himself. (Abdul Razzaq 6282)"
"11316","(11316) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the voice at three times, at the funeral procession, when the two funeral prayers met, and when reciting the Qur’an. The Qur’an.\n(Abu Dawud 2449. Hakim 116)"
"11317","(11317) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Sulaym, on the authority of Bilal bin Yahya, on the authority of Hudhayfă, who said: The Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of the obituary. (Ahmad 5/406, Tirmidhi 986)"
"11318","(11318) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The obituary is a matter of the pre-Islamic era."
"11319","(11319) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of his father, who said: Al-Rabi’ bin Khathim advised not Be kind to me, and ask me to my Lord in peace."
"11320","(11320) On the authority of Abdou bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, he said: I heard Abu Wa’il say upon his death: If I die, then Call anyone by me."
"11321","(11321) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Abu Misra advised his brother not to give the call to prayer. I have Uhud, Abu Ishaq said, and thus he instructed Alqamiya Al-Aswad."
"11322","(11322) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Ali ibn Mudarik, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, that I advise that you do not call anyone to me, for I fear that the mourning will be a matter of the pre-Islamic era."
"11323","(11323) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Umayyah, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, who said: Abraham said: If you are four, then do not give the call to prayer. Sunday"
"11324","(11324) Abu Nu`aym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Thawair, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that Ali ibn Hussein commanded that you not inform anyone about me."
"11325","(11325) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Asim ibn Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that if he died, he would have a dead death. People ignored him."
"11326","(11326) Al-Muharbibi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Khaythami, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafli, who said: If I die, do not announce the call to prayer for me. Sunday"
"11327","(11327) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of his brother Mutarrif, said: Do not call anyone to my funeral."
"11328","(11328) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of his father, he said: Do not give the call to prayer. At my funeral, the people of your mosque."
"11329","(11329) Hushaym told us, saying: Uthman bin Hakim informed us, on the authority of Kharijiyah bin Zayd, on the authority of his uncle, Yazid bin Thabit, who was older than Zaid, said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when we reached Al-Baqi’, we saw With a new grave, so he asked about it, and they said: So-and-so knew it. He said: Then he said: Did you not inform me of it? They said: You were saying, “We thought that we would call you to prayer.” He said: “Do not do so. I do not know that any of you who died was dead while you were there.” You have informed me of it, for indeed, your blessings upon him have mercy.\n(Bukhari 42. Ahmad 4/388)"
"11330","(11330) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, that he did not see any harm in a man giving the call to prayer. His intimate and friend at the funeral."
"11331","(11331) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Urwah, that Abu Hurairah was The call to prayer is given and he passes by the mosque and says, “Abdullah was called and he responded,” or “The Mother of God was called and she answered,” but no. He stays with her except a few of them."
"11332","(11332) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abi Hayyan, on the authority of his father, who said: Amr bin Maymun was a truthful person. To Al-Rabi’ ibn Khuthaym. When he became heavy, Amr said to the mother of the son of Al-Rabi’ ibn Khuthaym, “Inform me if he dies.” She said: Indeed, he said: If I am dead, so do not let anyone feel me, and ask me to my Lord in a request. He said, so Amr spent the night in the shops of Bani Thawr until the morning. So he witnessed it."
"11333","(11333) Muhammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he did not see It is unfortunate that a truthful one should pronounce the call to prayer for the dead, and he said: They only disliked an obituary like the obituary of the pre-Islamic era, an obituary. So-and-so"
"11334","(11334) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Nu’man, who said: When Ali was invited to A funeral, he said: Indeed, we will stand, and nothing is prayed upon a person except his own deeds."
"11335","(11335) Sa`id bin Yahya al-Himyari told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Husayn, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamiya bin Sahl, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to visit the poor people of Medina and witness Their funerals when they died. He said: Then a woman from among the family died, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Then She came, so call me to her. He said, “So they came to call him to the call to prayer, but they found him sleeping, and he had gone away during the night, so they thought to wake him up.” And the darkness of the night and the creatures of the earth feared for him, so when morning came he asked about her, and they said: O Messenger of God, we have come to you to call you to prayer. We found you sleeping and we hated to wake you and we feared for you because of the darkness of the night and the vermin of the earth. He said: So we buried you. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, walked to her grave and prayed for her and said “Allahu Akbar” four times. (Hakim 466)"
"11336","(11336) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, who said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace be upon him, Abu Bakr and Omar walking in front of the funeral procession. (Abu Dawud 3171, Tirmidhi 1007)"
"11337","(11337) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Salim, who said: I saw Ibn Umar walking in front of the funeral procession."
"11338","(11338) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of Abu Hazim, who said: I saw Abu Hurairah And Al-Hassan bin Ali walked in front of the funeral."
"11339","(11339) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Salih, the guardian of the twins, who said: I saw Abu Hurairah Abu Qatada, Ibn Umar and Abu Asid walked in front of the funeral procession."
"11340","(11340) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, he said: They were the companions of Muhammad May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, they walk in front of the funeral procession, and even when they are far from it, they stand up and wait for it."
"11341","(11341) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I saw Alqamiya and the lions walking in front of the funeral procession."
"11342","(11342) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I saw Salim and Al-Qasim walking in front of the funeral procession."
"11343","(11343) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I asked Muhammad about walking in front of a funeral procession, and he said: I do not know about it. Valiantly, he said: Al-Qasim and Salem were doing it."
"11344","(11344) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Anas: In the funeral, you are mourners for it, walking. In front of it and behind it, and to its right and to its left."
"11345","(11345) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Abu Malik told us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, he said: I walked with Al-Hasan bin Ali, Abu Hurairah, and Ibn al-Zubayr in front of the funeral. (Bayhaqi 27)"
"11346","(11346) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Al-Manyal, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, he said: A relative succeeded her. And in front of her is near, and to her left is near, and to her right is near."
"11347","(11347) Abu Khalid Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I saw Ibn Umar and Ubaid bin Umair walking. Imam of the funeral."
"11348","(11348) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Al-Aqqar ibn Al-Mughirah, he said: I was I was walking behind the funeral procession, then Abu Hurairah came and put my vertebrae between his two fingers, then he pushed me until I came in front of The funeral"
"11349","(11349) Yahya bin Saeed and Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Suwayd bin He negligently said: The angels walk behind the funeral procession. (Abdul Razzaq 6266)"
"11350","(11350) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Amir bin Jushayb and others from the Levant, who said: Abu Al-Darda': One of the full rewards of a funeral is for its family to mourn it and walk behind it."
"11351","(11351) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ammar, who said: Ibn Mu’mar said in the funeral of Abu Misra: Walk behind the funeral of Abu Misra, for he used to walk behind funerals."
"11352","(11352) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Abu Qalababi, not bitter, making the funerals His right hand"
"11353","(11353) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ibn Abza, he said: I was at a funeral, and Abu Bakr and Omar were in front of it and Ali was walking behind it. He said, I came to Ali, so I told him that it is better to walk behind her, or to walk in front of her, because I see you walking behind her, and these are two walks. In front of her, he said: So he said to me: They have learned that walking behind her is better than in front of her, like the congregational prayer for a feat. But they are two facilitators who love to make things easy for people. (Ahmad 1/971 Tahawi 483)"
"11354","(11354) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yahya al-Jabir, on the authority of Abu Majid, he said: I asked Ibn Masoud about walking. With the funeral, he said: Walking short of a trot, the funeral is followed, not followed, there is no one to lead it with it. (Musnad 356)"
"11355","(11355) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Murih bin Masruq, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: For every nation there is an offering, and the offering of these nations is their dead, so put your dead within your hands."
"11356","(11356) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Abu al-Nu`man, who said: I heard Abu Imamah say: Because I do not go out with her, I love Until I walk in front of her."
"11357","(11357) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Salil, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, who said: For the one who walks in The funeral is two qirats, and the passenger gets one qirat."
"11358","(11358) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abbas al-Hamdani, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, who said: I saw Ibn Umar on a mule. Riding in front of the funeral."
"11359","(11359) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, who said: I saw Abu Bakr in The funeral of Abd al-Rahman bin Samra on his mule."
"11360","(11360) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him at the funeral of Ibn Al-Dahdah, and he was riding on a horse, and he was standing with him while we were around him.\n(Muslim 664, Abu Dawud 3170)"
"11361","(11361) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Jabbar Al-Tai, who said: I saw Ibn Abbas at the funeral of his mother. Musab Ali has a Qumra donkey."
"11362","(11362) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Jabbar al-Tai, who said: I saw Ibn Abbas at a funeral. So he mentioned something like it."
"11363","(11363) Ibn Abi Zaydah and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: I saw a comment on A mule walks in front of the funeral procession, and Abu Muawiyah said: Ali is a white mule, walking behind the funeral procession."
"11364","(11364) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Na’im, who said: I saw Abu Wael at Khaythamah’s funeral. Riding on a donkey, he says, “We made you sad,” or a similar word."
"11365","(11365) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Dinar, who said: He said: I saw Ata’ walking in front of the funeral procession, riding."
"11366","(11366) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, who said: I saw Al-Hassan riding in front of the funeral procession."
"11367","(11367) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I saw Sharih riding at my father’s funeral. Easy way"
"11368","(11368) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ubaid Allah Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Ziyad bin Jubayr bin Hayya Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Abiyya, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bai, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: The rider is behind the funeral procession, and the walker Wherever he wants from her, and the child is prayed over. (Ahmad 4/248, Abu Dawud 3172)"
"11369","(11369) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hammam Al-Sakouni, who is Al-Walid ibn Qays, on the authority of Abu Birah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought with an animal while he was at his funeral, but he did not ride, so when he left, he mounted. (Abu Dawud 3169. Hakim 355)"
"11370","(11370) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I said to your people: Is it objectionable to walk behind a funeral procession? He said: No, it is disliked to walk in front of them."
"11371","(11371) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, he said: Abu Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, he said: If the men who ride during a funeral knew what the men who walk had to do, they would not have ridden."
"11372","(11372) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Rashid bin Saad, on the authority of Thawban, that he saw a man riding in a funeral procession. So he took the reins of his animal and began to curb it, and said: You will ride while the servants of God walk."
"11373","(11373) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They hated the rider to walk. In front of her"
"11374","(11374) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. He said: A passenger at a funeral is like someone sitting in his house."
"11375","(11375) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin did not walk in front of the funeral procession."
"11376","(11376) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The passenger at a funeral is like the person sitting in his house."
"11377","(11377) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Burda, on the authority of Abu Musa, who said: He passed by the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, greeted his funeral while it was being churned just as clay is churned, and he said: You must be intentional in your funerals.\n(Ahmad 4/4061 Ibn Majah 1479)"
"11378","(11378) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: Hasten with the funeral, for if it is righteous, it is good for you to present it to him, and if it is not that, then evil. You put it off your necks. (Bukhari 1315, Muslim 651)"
"11379","(11379) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Uyaynah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: He While I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, I saw him almost covering the funeral with sand. (Abu Dawud 31751. Ahmad 5/37)"
"11380","(11380) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Salama Ibn Alqamiya, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Imran Ibn Husayn recommended, He said: When I die, hasten, and do not become Judaizers like the Jews and Christians."
"11381","(11381) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, who said: Yahya bin Abi Rashid narrated to me. Al-Nasri said: Omar said when the death of his son came to him: If you go out, walk quickly with me. (Ibn Saad 358)"
"11382","(11382) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Hurry me to my Lord."
"11383","(11383) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Zaid al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, who said: If a man is to be cut off, He is vast in the funeral, but he does not reach it, or almost does not reach it."
"11384","(11384) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: When I die, hasten with me."
"11385","(11385) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, he said: I heard Abu Wa’il say upon his death: If I die So they quickly walked with me."
"11386","(11386) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Thuwair, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, that Ali ibn Husayn advised, “Hurry me up.” Walking"
"11387","(11387) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Amara bin Zazan, on the authority of Makhoul al-Azdi, who said: Ibn Umar heard a man say: Be gentle with her - May God have mercy on you - and he said: Be converted to Judaism, so that you may hasten with it, or I will return."
"11388","(11388) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was said: Rejoice with your funerals, And do not move therein like the animals of the Jews."
"11389","(11389) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad that they used to like to hasten At the funeral"
"11390","(11390) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Mu’tamir, he said: We were at a funeral, and when Al-Hasan saw one of them, he was Delaying, he said: Go, do not withhold your death."
"11391","(11391) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh, he said Abu Karb, or Abu Harb, told us on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr that he told him that his father advised him. He said: So you You carried me on the bed, so walk with me, walking between the two walks, and be behind the funeral procession, for its front is for the angels, and its back For the children of Adam."
"11392","(11392) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: No. Follow the funeral procession of the Christians."
"11393","(11393) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ali al-Azdi, who said: I saw Ibn Umar at his funeral. So they carried the four sides of the bed, starting with the right-hand side, then he moved away from it, and one side of it was like a dog's kennel."
"11394","(11394) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Do not care which side of the bed you start on."
"11395","(11395) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Mandal, on the authority of Ja`far bin Abi al-Mughairi, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: If you are able, start with the pillar next to his right hand, then circumambulate the bed. Otherwise, stay close to it."
"11396","(11396) Malik bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abu Awani, on the authority of Ja’far bin Iyas, who said: I saw Al-Hasan following a funeral procession. So he carried and placed the bed on its left side, then he turned around and carried the front of the bed on its right side, then he moved back and placed the back of the bed on The right side, then he turned and placed the back of the bed on the left side, then left it."
"11397","(11397) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ubaid bin Nastas, who said: We were with Abu Ubaidah. Ibn Abdullah at a funeral, and he said: Abdullah said: If one of you is at a funeral, he should carry all sides of the bed. It is part of the Sunnah, then to do it voluntarily, or to leave it alone."
"11398","(11398) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abbad bin Mansour, on the authority of Abu al-Muzzam, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: Whoever carried The funeral is three, and he has fulfilled his rights."
"11399","(11399) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Amir bin Jushayb and others from the Levant, who said: Abu Al-Darda': Part of the full reward for a funeral is to have its family mourn it, to carry its four corners, and to perform the funeral procession. In the grave."
"11400","(11400) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, with a funeral procession, and with it a woman. He did not leave until she disappeared into the houses."
"11401","(11401) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibn Mughaffal, who said: Omar said: Do not have a woman follow me."
"11402","(11402) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When they brought out the funeral procession, they closed the door on the women."
"11403","(11403) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muthanna bin Sa`id, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Muntashir, who said: It was stolen and no prayer was prayed for. A funeral with a woman."
"11404","(11404) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Zayd, who said: My father was There was a house in which there was a funeral procession. He ordered the door to be opened and Al-Awwad entered. When he came out with the funeral procession, he ordered the door of the house to be closed and it was closed. A woman follows her."
"11405","(11405) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We were forbidden to follow his funeral procession. He saw us with her.\n(Ibn Majah 1583. Tabarani 12)"
"11406","(11406) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: They disliked that women follow Funerals"
"11407","(11407) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan ibn Salih informed us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Suwayd said: A woman should not leave the door of the house with the funeral procession."
"11408","(11408) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Muawiyah bin Salih narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Qays narrated to us, saying: We were in There was a funeral at which Abu Umamah saw women at the funeral and drove them out."
"11409","(11409) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Masruq, who said: I saw him digging in the dirt. In the faces of women during the funeral and he says to them: Go back. If they return, he continues with the funeral, otherwise he goes back and leaves it."
"11410","(11410) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, he said: We are forbidden from following funerals, And he did not decide against us. (Muslim 646. Abu Dawud 3159)"
"11411","(11411) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Wahhab ibn Kaysan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata’, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was at a funeral and Omar saw a woman and shouted about her, so he said To him: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Leave her, O Omar, for the eye is weeping, the soul is afflicted, and the doom is near. (Ahmad 2/444, Hakim 381)"
"11412","(11412) Abu Bakr ibn Ayash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Jabbar al-Tai, who said: I witnessed the funeral of Umm Musaab ibn Al-Zubair, in which there is Ibn Abbas riding a Qumra donkey led by Qad, Abdullah bin Omar, and Ibn Amr. He said: Then they heard the sounds of shouting. He said: I said: O Ibn Abbas, he does this, and you are here? He said: Let us leave you, O mighty one, for God has made you laugh and make you cry."
"11413","(11413) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Dinar, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He came out for a funeral and they made They shouted at her, and Thabet came back and said to him: Good deeds give up truth for falsehood. He said: So he left."
"11414","(11414) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Salim and Al-Qasim walking in front of The funeral procession and the women behind it."
"11415","(11415) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, who said: Umm Salamah advised that Saeed bin Zaid may pray for her."
"11416","(11416) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Yunus bin Jubayr was instructed to pray On him is Anas bin Malik."
"11417","(11417) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Husayn: That Ubayd instructed that the lions should pray over him."
"11418","(11418) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that Abu Misra recommended that the prayer be prayed over him. Judge of Muslims, Shurayh."
"11419","(11419) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Al-Harith advised that May the peace be upon him, Abdullah bin Yazid."
"11420","(11420) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I have not known that anyone has more right to pray over anyone except To leave a will for the dead, and if the dead do not leave a will, the best of his family may pray for him."
"11421","(11421) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Muharib, that Umm Salamah instructed that he pray Ali is like the Imam."
"11422","(11422) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, who said: The imam is more deserving of the one who prays. On the funeral."
"11423","(11423) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: She went with Abraham to his funeral, and he was her guardian, so he sent for an imam. The living one, so he prayed for her."
"11424","(11424) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of his uncle Ghannam bin Talq, who said: Abu Burda, his servant, witnessed Shahad, so he ordered the Imam of Al-Hayy to come forward. Aliyah"
"11425","(11425) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Sa’ib, he said: Ibrahim’s son died. Al-Taymiyyah, so Ibrahim Al-Nakha’i witnessed her funeral, so Ibrahim Al-Nakha’i ordered the imam of Al-Tayyim to pray over her, and he said: This is the Sunnah."
"11426","(11426) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muslim, who said: I saw Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla. Abdullah bin Hakim came before his mother and was the living imam."
"11427","(11427) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafla, who said: The Imam has more right."
"11428","(11428) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Jarir, who said: The Imam comes forward."
"11429","(11429) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of al-Aswad, that it was It is given at funerals according to the Sunnah."
"11430","(11430) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I used to give priority to the lions. Funerals, Abraham said: He was their imam."
"11431","(11431) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, who said: A son of Abi Ma’shar died, but the imam was not present, so he said: So that whoever was praying after the imam should come forward."
"11432","(11432) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Salim, al-Qasim, Tawus, Mujahid, and Ata that they They were presenting the imam to the funeral procession."
"11433","(11433) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of his uncle, who said: Talhah and Zubayd witnessed the death of a woman related to them. To them, they presented the Imam of the Living."
"11434","(11434) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to give precedence to the Imams. Their funerals"
"11435","(11435) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The guardian takes precedence over the funeral of the one he loves."
"11436","(11436) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad and Alqamiya, who said: The Imam advances."
"11437","(11437) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaidullah, that Alqamiya used to lead the funeral prayers of a living person, and he was not an imam."
"11438","(11438) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Anis bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of his father, that a funeral took place, so Ibn Omar stood up and said: Where is the guardian of this funeral to pray over it before the sun rises?"
"11439","(11439) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Anbasa Al-Wazzan, who said: Abu Lubabi narrated to us, he said: I prayed with my father. A kitten at his funeral, and the sun was on the outskirts of the walls."
"11440","(11440) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Husayn, that his servants were commanded to pray He was wearing a black one. He said: So they brought him before the sun had set. He said: So the prayer was performed over him before the sun had set."
"11441","(11441) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far bin Burqan, on the authority of Maimun, who said: Ibn Umar used to dislike performing the funeral prayer. When the sun rises and when it sets."
"11442","(11442) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr, who said: Jabir bin Zayd was asked: Do you bury the funeral? When the sun rises or sets, or some of it sets, he said: No."
"11443","(11443) Ma’an narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: It is disliked to pray at a funeral after the afternoon prayer and after Fajr"
"11444","(11444) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad liked to pray over the funeral, then He prayed the afternoon prayer, but he disliked performing the funeral prayer after the afternoon prayer."
"11445","(11445) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, who said: I asked Al-Hasan about performing funeral prayers after the afternoon prayer, and he said: Yes, then. It was pure and white, so when it approaches the road to return, do not pray over it until the sun sets."
"11446","(11446) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Hafs, who said: Abdullah bin When it was a funeral, Omar prayed the afternoon prayer, then said: Hurry with it before the sun rises."
"11447","(11447) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abi Malik, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ash’ath, On the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin, they said: If the funeral comes and the obligatory prayer is in progress, he should begin with the obligatory prayer."
"11448","(11448) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, that he attended a funeral and I attended The prayer began with the obligatory prayer."
"11449","(11449) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It begins with what is written."
"11450","(11450) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: A son of mine died. He said: So he said: Ibn Sirin is for me if you can. That you take it out at a time when the prayer is prayed over it, then you perform the afternoon prayer."
"11451","(11451) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr bin Haram, who said: Jabir bin Zaid was asked about funerals. Is he prayed for before or after the Maghrib prayer? He said: The funeral prayer should be performed before it, then the Maghrib prayer should be performed."
"11452","(11452) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Bakr, who said: When you carry the funeral, then glorify it as long as you carry it."
"11453","(11453) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, he said: When he is carried, he says in the name of God and glorifies what he has carried."
"11454","(11454) Muadh bin Muadh told us, on the authority of Abu Khaldi, he said: I saw Al-Hasan praying over the funeral of Abu Raja’ Al-Atardi. On a donkey."
"11455","(11455) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not think there was any harm in a woman praying over him. A funeral while she was standing on her donkey."
"11456","(11456) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah bin Murra, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: He is not one of us who slaps his cheeks, rips his pockets, and invokes the supplications of the people of the pre-Islamic era. (Bukhari 1294, Muslim 165)"
"11457","(11457) Waki’ and Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, On the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: He who strikes the cheeks, rips the pockets, and makes supplications is not among us. People of pre-Islamic times (Bukhari 1297, Tirmidhi 999)"
"11458","(11458) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Iyad Al-Ash’ari, who said when Abu Musa fainted, he cried out His wife. When he woke up, he said: Did you not know what I told you? She said: When he died, you did not shout at him, so we said: What did he say to you? She said: He said: He is not one of us who cuts his hair, or shaves his hair, or cuts his hair. (Muslim 1000, Abu Dawud 3122)"
"11459","(11459) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Saham bin Munjab, on the authority of Al-Qartha’, he said: When it became heavy Abu Musa, his wife shouted at him, and he said: To her, did you not know what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said? She said: Yes, then she remained silent, then she was told: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say? He said: So she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, has cursed those who shave, pierce, and flog. (Ahmad 4/4051 An-Nasa’i 1994)"
"11460","(11460) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said, when Khalid ibn Al-Walid died, the wives of his children gathered together. Al-Mughirah was crying over him, so it was said to Umar, “Send for them, for they will not inform you of anything that you disliked.” He said Then Omar said: And they should not shed any of their tears for Abu Suleiman unless there is a rain or because of anxiety."
"11461","(11461) Abu Usamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: Al-Qasim and Makhul narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Imamah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed the face of the one who is unjust and the one who is harsh on her face. (Ibn Majah 1585. Darmi 2476)"
"11462","(11462) Waki’ and Ali bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: I forbade making a sound in the time of calamity that scratches faces, rips one’s pockets, and makes a devil’s ringing. (Bayhaqi 69)"
"11463","(11463) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, he said: Huraim narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: None of us shave, shave, or cut ourselves."
"11464","(11464) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hilal ibn Khabab, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, who said: Food is Dying is a matter of the pre-Islamic era, and mourning is a matter of the pre-Islamic era."
"11465","(11465) Fadalah bin Husayn narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: Three matters The ignorant woman is not one of them, and wailing and slaughtering camels at the time of the calamity is not one of them. The misfortune"
"11466","(11466) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Qays, who said: I realized that Omar bin Abdul Aziz prevented the family of The dead people say, “They will be punished and fined.”"
"11467","(11467) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik ibn Mughal, on the authority of Talha, who said: Jarir came to Omar and said: Will he mourn before you? On the dead? He said: No. He said: So do the women gather with you to attend to the dead and give food? He said: Yes. Then he said: That is the mourning."
"11468","(11468) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, he said: A man was walking behind the funeral procession and reciting Surah Al-Waqi’ah, so he was asked. Abraham thought about that."
"11469","(11469) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I saw Al-Hasan and Muhammad at a funeral, but they did not carry it until they returned."
"11470","(11470) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Al-Bara’ bin Yazid narrated to us, saying: I saw Al-Sha’bi at a funeral. I saw him walking behind her, not carrying her, and not touching her sticks until they were placed on the edge of the grave. Then he stepped aside and sat down. He was an old man."
"11471","(11471) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Mu’awiyah bin Salih narrated to us, saying: Habib bin Ubaid Al-Kala’i narrated to me. On the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja’i, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He says about the dead: O God, forgive him, have mercy on him, protect him, pardon him, honor his abode, widen his entrance, and wash him. With water, ice, and hail, and purify it from sins as a white garment is purified from filth. O God, replace it with a better abode than A home and a husband better than his wife, and a family better than his family, and admit him to Paradise, and save him from Hell, or he said: protect him. The torment of the grave until I wished I were him.\n O God, forgive him, have mercy on him, pardon him, honor his abode, widen his entrance, and wash him with water, snow, and hail. And purify him from sins as a white garment is purified from filth. O God, replace him with a house better than his house and a husband better than his. Marry him, and give him a better family than his family, and admit him to Paradise, and save him from Hell. Protect him from the torment of the Fire. (Muslim 662. Ahmad 6/23)"
"11472","(11472) Abu Usama told us, he said: Hisham al-Dastawai told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Ibrahim Al-Ansari, on the authority of his father, said that he heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say in the prayer for the dead: O God, forgive our living and our dead, our witnesses and our absent, our males and our females, our young and our old. (Tirmidhi 1024, Nasa’i 2113)"
"11473","(11473) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Jalas, on the authority of Uthman bin Shamas, who said: We were with my father. Then Marwan passed by him and told him some of your hadith on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he went on and then returned. So we said: Now it happens to him. He said: How did you hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying over the funeral? He said: I heard it. He says: You guided her to Islam, and you took her soul, knowing its secrets and its public ones. We have brought you as intercessors, so forgive her.\n(Abu Dawud 3192; Ahmad 2/363)"
"11474","(11474) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of a man from the people of Mecca, on the authority of Abu Salama, and on the authority of Ali Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in prayer Funeral: O God, forgive our living and our dead, our male and female, our witness and our absent, our young and our old, O God. Whoever of us You bring alive, let him live as a Muslim, and whoever of us You take to death, let him die as a Muslim. (Ibn Majah 358)"
"11475","(11475) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik, who said: When Abu Bakr prayed for the dead He said: Oh God, your servant has made his family, money, and family safe from him, and the sin is great, and you are the Forgiving, the Merciful."
"11476","(11476) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Omar used to say in the prayer upon him: It was evening, so he said: Oh God, your servant has passed the evening, and if it was morning, he said: Oh God, your servant has renounced this world and left it in the morning. To Him and You dispensed with Him and He became in need of You. He bore witness that there is no god but You, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger. So forgive him his sin."
"11477","(11477) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, he said: It was Ali He says in the prayer for the dead: O God, forgive our living and our dead, and reconcile our hearts, and reconcile our lives, and make Our hearts are upon the hearts of our choices. O God, forgive him. O God, have mercy on him. O God, return him to something better than what he was in. O God. Excuse me"
"11478","(11478) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: I was at the funeral of sheep, and a man among them narrated to me that he said: I heard Abu Musa prayed over a dead person, so he said “Allahu Akbar” and said, “O God, forgive him as he asked for your forgiveness and give him what he asked of you and increase him of your bounty.”"
"11479","(11479) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: Abdullah bin Salam said the prayer The funeral person should say, “O God, forgive our living and our dead, our young and our old, our males and our females, and our witnesses.” And those who are absent from us, O God, whomever You cause to die among them, cause him to die in faith, and whomever You spare among them, cause him to remain in Islam."
"11480","(11480) Affan bin Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Awan narrated to us, he said: Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Amr bin Ghaylan, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda’, that he used to say about the dead, O God, forgive our living and our dead. Muslims, O God, forgive the Muslim men and women, the believing men and believing women, and reconcile between them and bring harmony between them. Their hearts and set their hearts over the hearts of their choices. O God, forgive so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, his sins, and join him to the Prophet Muhammad. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, O God, raise his rank among those who are guided, and make him succeed in his successor among those who left behind, and make His book is in the highest, and forgive us and him, Lord of the worlds. O God, do not deprive us of his reward, and do not lead us astray after him."
"11481","(11481) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Zayd Al-Ammi, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq Al-Naji, he said: I asked Abu Sa’id about The funeral prayer, and he said: We used to say: O God, You are our Lord and His Lord. You created him, provided for him, kept him alive, and sufficed him, so forgive him. To us and to him, and do not deprive us of his reward, and do not lead us astray after him."
"11482","(11482) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to say during the funeral: May God bless him and bless him and forgive him and bring him into the basin of Your Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said. Of much standing and much speaking, I did not understand anything other than that."
"11483","(11483) Muhammad bin Fudail told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: I asked Mujahid about praying for the dead, and Mujahid said: We We say, O God, You created him and You guided him to Islam and You took his soul and You know best his secret. We have come to intercede for him, so forgive him."
"11484","(11484) Ishaq bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hariz, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Awf, on the authority of Ibn Luhayy. Al-Hawzani said that he witnessed the funeral of Sharhabil bin Al-Samat, and Habib bin Muslim Al-Fari came to us and came to us. Like the one who supervises us for a long time, and he said: Be diligent in supplication for your brother, and let him be in what you supplicate for him; O God, forgive this upright and Muslim soul, and make it among those who repent and follow Your path, protecting it from torment. Hell, and seek victory from God against your enemy."
"11485","(11485) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not permit us. May God bless him and grant him peace, nor did Abu Bakr, nor Omar say anything about praying for the dead. (Ibn Majah 1501. Ahmad 3/357)"
"11486","(11486) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of thirty The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not do anything regarding the funeral prayer."
"11487","(11487) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no temporary supplication in praying for the dead, so pray Whatever you want"
"11488","(11488) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab and Al-Shu’bi, who said: It is not for the dead. A temporary supplication."
"11489","(11489) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, who said: I asked Muhammad about praying for the dead, and he said: We do not know about it. Something temporary, pray for the best of what you know."
"11490","(11490) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Suwayd, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, who said: Not in prayer. The dead person is a temporary thing."
"11491","(11491) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Musa al-Jinni, he said: I asked al-Hakam, al-Sha`bi, Ata’, and Mujahid, “Is it true?” Is praying for the dead a temporary thing? They said: No, but you are an intercessor, so intercede with the best of what you know."
"11492","(11492) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Abu Salama, who said: I heard Al-Shu’abi say regarding the prayer for the dead, there is no There is something temporary in it."
"11493","(11493) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said regarding the first takbir, it begins with praising God. The second is a prayer for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, the third is a supplication for the dead, and the fourth is For delivery."
"11494","(11494) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, that when he prayed for A dead person begins with the praise of God and sends blessings upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then he says: O God, forgive our living. And our dead, and reconcile our hearts, and make peace between us, and make our hearts like the hearts of our choices."
"11495","(11495) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, that a man asked He came to Abu Hurairah and said: How do you perform the funeral prayer? Abu Hurairah said: I will tell you for the life of God that I say the greatest, then I will pray for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then I will say: Oh God. Your male or female servant worships you, not associating anything with you, and you know him best. If he is a doer of good, increase his benevolence. And if he is wrong, then forgive him. O God, do not test us after him, and do not deprive us of his reward."
"11496","(11496) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I heard him say: In the first, there is praise for Ali. God Almighty, and in the second is a prayer upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and in the third is a supplication for the dead, and in the fourth. Thank you"
"11497","(11497) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: I heard Abu Imamah narrating Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said One of the Sunnahs in the funeral prayer is to recite the opening of the book, then pray for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the supplication is recited for the dead person until he finishes, and you should not recite it except once, then say it to yourself.\n(Abdul Razzaq 6428 and Ibn al-Jaroud 540)"
"11498","(11498) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He used to raise his hand. In every takbeer on the funeral."
"11499","(11499) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Anas, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz used to raise His hand in every takbeer of the funeral takbeer."
"11500","(11500) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He raises his hands in every “Allahu Akbar” and those behind it raise their hands."
"11501","(11501) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qais, on the authority of Musa bin Nu’aym, the client of Zayd bin Thabit, who said: It is Sunnah to raise your hands in every takbeer of the funeral."
"11502","(11502) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Salim saying the takbir at his funeral four times. He raises his hands at every takbeer."
"11503","(11503) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Zayed, who said: I prayed behind Qais bin Abi Hazim Ali. A funeral procession, so he said “Allahu Akbar” four times, raising his hand in each “Allahu Akbar.”"
"11504","(11504) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdullah bin Juma’ al-Zuhri, who said: I saw Abraham when He prayed at the funeral. He raised his hands and said “Allahu Akbar,” then he did not raise his hands for the rest of the time, and he said “Allahu Akbar” by four."
"11505","(11505) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, that he used to raise his hand on the first Takbeerah for the funeral."
"11506","(11506) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to raise his hand with everyone. Takbeerah for the funeral."
"11507","(11507) Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, he said: Muhammad used to raise his hands in prayer, and when He bowed, and whenever he raised his head from bowing, he did that with all the takbir of the funeral."
"11508","(11508) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Naffa` ibn Muslim, who said: Suwayd used to say “Allahu Akbar” At our funerals, he used to raise his hand at the first takbeer."
"11509","(11509) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: I prayed behind Qais bin Abi Hazim Ali. A funeral, and he would continue it while saying “Allahu Akbar.”"
"11510","(11510) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahil bin Hanif, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Sibbaq, that he told him that he saw Sahl bin Hanif praying over a dead person, so he recited at the beginning of Takbeerah with the Mother of the Qur’an, then he continued to say Takbirah between that, until when Takbeerah remained, he recited the Tashahid. He recited the prayer, then he said “Allahu Akbar” and left."
"11511","(11511) Abbad bin Al-Awwam narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Abu Raja’, on the authority of Abu Al-‘Aryan Al-Hadha, he said: I prayed behind Al-Hasan bin Ali was at his funeral, and when he finished, I took him by the hand and said, “How did you do?” He said: I recited to her the opening of the book."
"11512","(11512) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of a man from Hamdan, that Abdullah bin Masoud He recited to her with the opening of the book."
"11513","(11513) Azhar al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Al-Hasan used to recite the opening of the Book in every exaltation of God. The funeral"
"11514","(11514) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Salama, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Recite the first two takbeers with the opening of the book."
"11515","(11515) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, that he used to recite the first two takbeers in Praying for the dead with the opening of the Book, and if they dictate to him to supplicate in it, he supplicates in it."
"11516","(11516) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: I heard Abu Imamah narrating Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said It is Sunnah in the funeral prayer to recite the opening of the book."
"11517","(11517) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahil bin Hanif, on the authority of Ubaid bin al-Sibbaq, that he told him that he saw Sahl bin Hanif praying over a dead person, and he recited at the beginning of Takbeerah on the Mother of the Qur’an."
"11518","(11518) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Sa’id, that Ibn Abbas recited at his funeral and spoke loudly, and said : I only did it so that you would know that there is a recitation in it."
"11519","(11519) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Ma’bad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he used to listen to people With praise, and he says “Allahu Akbar” for the funeral three times."
"11520","(11520) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd ibn Talha, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he recited the Fatih to her. The book"
"11521","(11521) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Hashim Al-Wasiti, on the authority of the distinguished servant of Omar that the one who He prayed for Abu Bakr, or Omar recited the Fatihah of the Book over him."
"11522","(11522) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar did not recite the prayer for Ali. The dead"
"11523","(11523) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, that he did not recite the prayer for the dead."
"11524","(11524) Abd al-A’la and Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu al-Minhal, who said: I asked Aba al-A’liyah about the Qara’ites. Concerning the funeral prayer with the Fatihah of the Book, he said: I did not think that the Fatihah of the Book was read except in a prayer in it. Bowing and prostration."
"11525","(11525) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father, who said: I said to Fadalah bin Ubaid, “Should it be recited to me?” Is the dead thing something? He said: No."
"11526","(11526) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Burda, on the authority of his father, he said: He said to him: A man who was recited at the funeral procession with the opening of the book? He said: Do not read."
"11527","(11527) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’ about reciting the Qur’an at the funeral, and he said: We have not heard. This is nothing but a hadith."
"11528","(11528) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abdullah bin Iyas, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu al-Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi said: There are no Qur’anic Qur’an in the funeral."
"11529","(11529) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zam`a, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, and Ata` that they used to deny Recitation at the funeral."
"11530","(11530) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Suwayd, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah? He said: I do not know of any recitation in it."
"11531","(11531) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Maqil, who said: I asked a person in charge of the funeral procession to recite it, or to pray for him. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I did not know."
"11532","(11532) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Sara narrated to us, saying: I asked Salim. So I said: Reciting at the funeral? He said: No recitation at the funeral."
"11533","(11533) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Ma’bad, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he used to listen to people. With praise and he says “Allahu Akbar” at the funeral."
"11534","(11534) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Hakim, he said: Kharijiyah ibn Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of his uncle, Zayd ibn It is established that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed over the grave of a woman and said the “Allahu Akbar” four times."
"11535","(11535) Saeed bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl, On the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed over the grave of a woman and said the “Allahu Akbar” four times."
"11536","(11536) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sulaym bin Hayyan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Mina, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed for Asahmah al-Najashi, and he recited the “Allahu Akbar” for him four times. (Bukhari 3879. Muslim 64)"
"11537","(11537) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Al-Baqi’ led the Negus in prayer and recited the takbir four times."
"11538","(11538) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Negus has died, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions went out to Al-Baqi’, so we lined up behind him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came forward and said the “Allahu Akbar” four times.\n(Bukhari 1333. Muslim 62)"
"11539","(11539) Hafs bin Ghayath and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abza, he said: Zainab bint Jahsh died, and Omar said four times over her. Then he asked the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who were He will enter her grave, so say: Who would enter upon her during her life?"
"11540","(11540) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Sila’, on the authority of Abd Khair, who said: He was arrested while he was He says “Allahu Akbar” four times."
"11541","(11541) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Umair ibn Sa`id, who said: I prayed behind Ali, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of Yazid ibn al-Mukaffif. He said “Allahu Akbar” to him four times."
"11542","(11542) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Umair, on the authority of Ali similar to him."
"11543","(11543) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah was asked about saying the takbeer at funerals, He said: All of this has been done, and I saw that the people had agreed on four things."
"11544","(11544) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, Sufyan, and Shu’bi, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, on the authority of Abu Atiyya, who said: Abdullah said: The takbeer for funerals is four times, with the takbir of going out."
"11545","(11545) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Mujar Abi Al-Hasan, who said: I prayed behind Al-Bara’ at his funeral and he said the takbir four times."
"11546","(11546) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, who said: A man asked him about The takbeer for the funeral, and he said: Four, so I said: Night and day are equal. He said: Then he said: Night and day are equal."
"11547","(11547) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zaid bin Talha, who said: I witnessed Ibn Abbas saying the takbeer at his funeral. Four"
"11548","(11548) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Thabit ibn Ubaid, that Zayd ibn Thabit said the takbir four times, and that Abba Huraira said “Allahu Akbar” four times."
"11549","(11549) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, on the authority of his father, he said: I prayed behind Abu Hurairah Ali. A funeral and he said the takbeer over it four times."
"11550","(11550) Hafs told us, on the authority of Atiyya bin Al-Harith Abi Ruq, on the authority of a servant of Al-Hasan bin Ali, that Al-Hasan bin Ali He prayed for Ali and said “Allahu Akbar” four times."
"11551","(11551) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar used to pronounce no more than four takbeers on The dead"
"11552","(11552) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Uthman bin Abdullah bin Mawhib, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit Like him"
"11553","(11553) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Maqil, he said: Ali said the takbir four times during his reign, except for Sahl ibn Hanif, for he said the takbir six times, then he turned around. To them, he said: It is early."
"11554","(11554) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said: We used to say “Allahu Akbar” to him. The dead five and six times, then we gathered in four takbeers."
"11555","(11555) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Aoun, that Muhammad said the “Allahu Akbar” four times."
"11556","(11556) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Ata, who said: I witnessed the death of Ibn Abbas, and Ibn al-Hanafi appointed him as governor. He said “Allahu Akbar” to him four times."
"11557","(11557) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, that he used to say takbir at the funeral. Four"
"11558","(11558) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Hijri, who said: I prayed with Abdullah bin Abi Awfa at his funeral, so he said the takbir. He said four times to her, then he stood up and bowed down until I thought he was saying “Allahu Akbar” five times. Then he greeted me and said: Did you see that I was saying “Allahu Akbar”? I say the Akbar five times. I only stood up as I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, standing up. (Ahmad 4/356; Abd al-Razzaq 6404)"
"11559","(11559) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdullah bin Juma’, who said: I saw Abraham, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. funeral, so he said the takbir four times."
"11560","(11560) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Zayed, who said: I prayed behind Qais bin Abi Hazim Ali. funeral, so he said the takbir four times."
"11561","(11561) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: Omar said, “Everyone has done it,” so they said: “Come, let us gather together.” It is something that those after us followed, so they said the takbeer for the funeral by four times."
"11562","(11562) Ismail bin Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, who said: I prayed behind and three people, so he said the takbir four times."
"11563","(11563) Ja`far ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Abu al-Khasib, that Suwayd prayed over a funeral procession and said the takbir four times."
"11564","(11564) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amir bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: Omar gathered the people and consulted them about it. Saying “Allahu Akbar” at the funeral. Some of them said, “Allah’s Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Allahu Akbar” five times, and some of them said, “Allah is Great” seven times. And some of them said, “Allahu Akbar” four times. He said, “So they gathered them to say four “Allahu Akbar” as the length of the prayer. (Abdul Razzaq 6395)"
"11565","(11565) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayd, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, he said: Ibrahim said: The companions of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said the takbeer at the funeral, then they agreed after that on four takbeers."
"11566","(11566) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Zayd ibn Arqam, that he prayed over a dead person and said “Allahu Akbar” He owes him five."
"11567","(11567) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: It was Zaid said the takbir at our funerals four times, and he said the takbir at his funeral five times, so I asked him, and he said: It was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, may God bless him and grant him peace, glorifies her. (Muslim 72. Abu Dawud 3189)"
"11568","(11568) Waki’ and Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Zirr, that Ibn Masoud said “Allahu Akbar” Ali a man from Baladan five times."
"11569","(11569) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Alqamiya ibn Qays, that he came from the Levant and said: To Abd By God, I saw Muadh bin Jabal and his companions in the Levant saying the “Allahu Akbar” at the funerals five times, so set a time for us to follow you on it. He said: Then Abdullah knocked for an hour, then said: Say “Allahu Akbar” (Allah is greater) as your imam said “Allahu Akbar” without time or number."
"11570","(11570) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, on the authority of a servant of Hudhaifa, On the authority of Hudhayfah, he said the takbeer at his funeral five times, adding more than one bow, then he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him.\n(Ahmad 5/406. Daraqutni 9)"
"11571","(11571) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of a writer of Ali, that Ali said “Allahu Akbar” to me. Five funeral."
"11572","(11572) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ayyub ibn al-Nu’man, who said: I prayed behind Zayd ibn Arqam at a funeral and he said the takbir. She has five."
"11573","(11573) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Sila’, on the authority of Abd Khair, who said: Ali used to say “Allahu Akbar” to his family. Badr six, and the Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, five, and the rest of the people four."
"11574","(11574) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Ma’bad, who said: Ibn Abbas used to gather people with praise. He says the takbir three times over the funeral."
"11575","(11575) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, who said: I prayed with Anas bin Malik at his funeral, and he said the takbeer over it three times. He did not say anything more to her, then he left."
"11576","(11576) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of al-Qasim, he said: My father informed me that he prayed over my funeral, and Jabir said to him: Ibn Zayd came forward and said the Akbar three times."
"11577","(11577) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. He greeted Hamza, so he said “Allahu Akbar” for her nine times, then he brought the last one and said “Allahu Akbar” for it seven times, then he brought the last one and said “Allahu Akbar” for it seven times. She had to do it five times until he finished with them, except that they were odd. (Bayhaqi 13. Ibn Saad 16)"
"11578","(11578) Abdullah bin Numayr and Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Yazid said: Ali prayed for Abu Qatada and he recited the takbir for him seven times."
"11579","(11579) It was narrated on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no more than seven takbeers, and no less than Four"
"11580","(11580) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed. He greeted Hamza and they began to raise themselves up with Hamza in their hands until he finished praying for them. (Ibn Saad 16. Abu Dawud 435)"
"11581","(11581) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed Ali Hamza, and he used to bring nine people, and they would be placed with him, and he would pray over them, then they would be taken up and left, and he would come. With nine others, and he continued like that until he prayed for them all."
"11582","(11582) Hushaym told us, saying: Husayn told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; That Ali prayed over Sahl bin Hanif, and he recited the takbeer six times."
"11583","(11583) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Suwayd, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, who said: It is not less than three. Takbirat, not more than seven."
"11584","(11584) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Ibn al-Asbaani, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal, on the authority of Ali, that He said the takbeer to Sahil bin Hanif six times. (Bukhari 4004)"
"11585","(11585) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Mughaffal, that Ali said the greatest thing to Saul bin Hanif six times."
"11586","(11586) Omar bin Ayyub Al-Mawsili told us, on the authority of Mughirah bin Ziyad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If you fear If you miss the funeral without having performed ablution, then perform tayammum and pray."
"11587","(11587) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zaara’i, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: If the funeral suddenly comes to you while you are... Without performing ablution, he performed tayammum and prayed for her."
"11588","(11588) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If the funeral suddenly comes to you and you are not there Ablution. If you have water, perform ablution and pray, and if you do not have water, perform ablution and pray."
"11589","(11589) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad and Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He performs tayammum if he fears missing out."
"11590","(11590) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you fear that you will miss the funeral, then perform tayammum. And pray."
"11591","(11591) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he fears that he will miss the prayer upon him. The funeral was performed with tayammum."
"11592","(11592) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He should perform tayammum if he fears missing out."
"11593","(11593) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyy told us on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: If you fear that you will miss Praying while you are not performing ablution, then perform tayammum."
"11594","(11594) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Salim, who said: He performs tayammum, and Al-Qasim said: He does not even pray over her. He performs ablution."
"11595","(11595) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He should not perform tayammum or pray except in a state of purity."
"11596","(11596) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man attending a funeral and fearing that he will miss the prayer for her. He said: He should not perform tayammum."
"11597","(11597) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He performs tayammum and prays upon him."
"11598","(11598) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man attending a funeral without having performed ablution, he said: He should pray over it."
"11599","(11599) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail and Muti’, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: He prayed for her, and Muti’ added in it, not There is no bowing or prostration in it."
"11600","(11600) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he did not judge What he missed of saying “Allahu Akbar” at the funeral."
"11601","(11601) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If you miss a takbeer, or two takbeers On the funeral procession, hasten and say the takbir of what you missed before it takes off."
"11602","(11602) Hammad bin Masadi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Qaridh bin Shaybah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, He said: Build on what he missed of saying “Allahu Akbar” at the funeral."
"11603","(11603) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: He magnifies what he has overtaken and makes up for what came before him, and he said Al-Hassan: He magnifies what came before him, and does not erase what came before it."
"11604","(11604) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi and Ata’, who said: Do not make up what you missed of the takbeer. On the funeral."
"11605","(11605) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Hammad, who said: He will judge."
"11606","(11606) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, who said: He ennobles what he overtakes, but does not fulfill what he fulfills. He missed it"
"11607","(11607) Abu Ahmad Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubair narrated to us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Yaqoub, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Hamid Ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: He makes up for what he missed of saying “Allahu Akbar” at the funeral."
"11608","(11608) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith, that he used to say: If a man comes to the funeral and has He preceded with some takbeer. He did not say takbeer until the imam said takbeer."
"11609","(11609) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who arrives at the funeral and they are praying over it. He said: He enters with them with great pride."
"11610","(11610) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he did not dare to pronounce the greeting. On the funeral."
"11611","(11611) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that when he prayed over the funeral He raised his hands and said “Allahu Akbar,” and when he finished, he greeted his right hand once."
"11612","(11612) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Umair bin Saeed, who said: Ali prayed for Yazid bin Al-Mukaffaf. So he said the takbir four times, and made a silent salutation on his right."
"11613","(11613) Waki’ and Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he used to greet the funeral procession with greetings."
"11614","(11614) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, who said: I prayed behind him at his funeral, so he greeted on the authority of His right hand when peace be upon you was finished."
"11615","(11615) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he used to greet the funeral with a sincere greeting."
"11616","(11616) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdul-Malik Ibn Iyas, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The salutation of forgetfulness And the funeral is one."
"11617","(11617) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abdul-Malik Ibn Iyas, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Greet the funeral. Peace be upon you"
"11618","(11618) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Hilal bin Mazyd, who said: I prayed behind Jabir bin Zayd, and he greeted me with salutations. The first is on his right, and the last is on his left."
"11619","(11619) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Ibn Sirin prayed and gave his salutations, so he listened to me. The funeral"
"11620","(11620) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, on the authority of his father, that he said: I prayed behind Abu Hurairah At a funeral procession, he said the takbeer over it four times, and made salutations on his right."
"11621","(11621) Waki’ and Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansur bin Hayyan, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr. He used to greet the funeral procession with salutations."
"11622","(11622) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He greets you automatically and on his face. And those behind the imam will respond."
"11623","(11623) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Harith, who said: I saw Amir praying over a funeral procession and he gave the salaam on his right, and on the authority of North"
"11624","(11624) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Qutbai, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Yahya, that when he prayed over a funeral He gave one salutation."
"11625","(11625) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, who said: I prayed with thirty of the sixty funeral corpses of the plague. Men and women. Then he said “Allahu Akbar” four times and said his salutations."
"11626","(11626) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Al-Ala’ narrated to me, saying: I prayed behind an alcoholic person at his funeral, so he greeted him. Greetings from his right hand."
"11627","(11627) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Asim, who said: I asked Ghanim. I said: Should I say the salutation during the funeral prayer? He said: Yes, are you not in prayer?"
"11628","(11628) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abi Al-Haytham, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he used to greet The funeral is on his right and on his left."
"11629","(11629) Abdullah bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Al-Miswar bin Makhramah used to testify. A funeral procession that did not sit until it was placed."
"11630","(11630) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that it was not He sits until the bed is made."
"11631","(11631) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn and Kathir bin Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawwi, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Many, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who narrated it, saying: If you are at a funeral, do not sit until the funeral is completed. The bed\n(Abu Dawud 31651, Ahmad 38)"
"11632","(11632) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, and Abu Habira, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that when He accompanied a funeral procession and did not sit until it was placed."
"11633","(11633) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When the bed is made, sit down."
"11634","(11634) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, who said: I saw Urwa ibn al-Zubayr at a funeral, so he leaned on A wall, so he started saying: Did the funeral procession begin? He did not sit until she was delivered."
"11635","(11635) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhayr, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim and Al-Shu’abi, who said: They were They hate to sit until the funeral procession is placed on the men’s shoulders."
"11636","(11636) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abu Hazim, who said: I walked with Al-Hasan bin Ali, Abu Hurairah, and Ibn al-Zubayr. When they reached the grave, they stood up and talked until the funeral was ready. When They sat down."
"11637","(11637) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, that he would not sit until he was placed. He said: Al-Hasan did not He sees harm in it."
"11638","(11638) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Waqid bin Amr bin Saad bin Muadh, he said: I was At my funeral, I did not sit until I was placed on the ground. Then I came to Nafi’ ibn Jubayr and sat next to him, and he said: Why did I not see you sitting? Until the funeral took place, and I said that because of a hadith that reached me on the authority of Abu Saeed, and Nafi’ said: Masoud bin Al-Hakam told me that Ali told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up, then sat down. (Muslim 83. Abu Dawud 3167)"
"11639","(11639) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Anis bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Ibn Umar and another man They sit down before the funeral takes place."
"11640","(11640) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, that al-Qasim and Salim were walking in front of the funeral procession. And they sit together."
"11641","(11641) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Saeed, that he saw Al-Hasan sitting before the funeral was placed on the grave."
"11642","(11642) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far and Amir, who said: There is no harm in sitting before it is placed. The funeral is in the grave."
"11643","(11643) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, he said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: We went out with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, at the funeral of a man from the Ansar, so we went to the grave, and when he was gone, he said: So the Messenger of God sat down. May God bless him and grant him peace, and we sat around him as if there were birds on our heads. (Abu Dawud, 3204, Ibn Khuzaymah 12)"
"11644","(11644) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Muwarriq Al-Ijli, who said: You are not just between two matters. Unless I find something similar to them in the sight of God, the easier of them both, then I sit in the funeral prayer."
"11645","(11645) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Sa`id al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw a father Huraira and Marwan were walking in front of the funeral procession, then they sat down, and Abu Sa`id al-Khudri came and said: Get up, Emir, for he has lost This, meaning Abu Hurairah, knew that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, followed the funeral procession, he would not even sit down. be placed\n(Bukhari 1310, Muslim 660)"
"11646","(11646) Ibn Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Al-Miswar ibn Makhrimah would not return until He is called to Him."
"11647","(11647) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: When you pray As for the funeral, you have fulfilled what you owed, so leave it alone with its family."
"11648","(11648) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir said: Walk with the funeral procession as long as you want, then come back if you wish."
"11649","(11649) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, that he did not see that they had permission and would say: What is their authority? On us"
"11650","(11650) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Nafi’, who said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr praying at my funeral, then He came back"
"11651","(11651) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: A man said to Nafi’: Was Ibn Umar returning from the funeral? Before the call was given to him after they had finished, he said: He would not return until the call was given to him."
"11652","(11652) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Two princes, but not two princes, a companion If the funeral prayer is performed over her, she will not return except with her permission, and the woman who is a pilgrim is with her when she is menstruating."
"11653","(11653) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Amiran and not With two orders: the funeral attendant and the menstruating woman in companionship."
"11654","(11654) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Umar, like him."
"11655","(11655) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Talha Al-Yami, who said: It was said that they were two princes, not two princes. With the two commands of the funeral for those who follow it, and for the pilgrimage woman to accompany her when she menstruates."
"11656","(11656) Abd al-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi al-Qassaf, who said: I was with my father. He was performing his funeral prayer, and when he prayed, he left. He said: So I said to him before you are called to prayer. He said: So he said: Are they the most important princes over us?"
"11657","(11657) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Aqeel, he said: I told him: Who should follow the funeral then? He said: No, but a man should be modest to return until permission is given to him."
"11658","(11658) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Mahfouz bin Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: Two things, but not two things: is the woman with a group and performs Hajj, or does she perform Umrah and is afflicted with something worse than menstruation? He said: Do not leave until you have purified yourself and you have given them permission. And the man who goes out with the funeral procession does not return until he is given permission, or They bury her, or hide her."
"11659","(11659) Marhum bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Muhammad, who said: I was with Al-Hasan at his funeral, and when he gave the call to prayer To them, I said to Al-Hasan, “He has granted them permission.” He said: “And permission has been given to us.”"
"11660","(11660) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: He follows the funeral procession as he sees fit and returns. If it seems to him"
"11661","(11661) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, similar to him."
"11662","(11662) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Amiran They are not of two orders: the man performs the funeral prayer and is not allowed to return except with the permission of its family, and the woman is with her. The people must menstruate before circumambulating the Kaaba on the Day of Sacrifice. They are not allowed to depart except with her permission."
"11663","(11663) Abdullah bin Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein Al-Mukhtab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, on the authority of Samurah bin Jundub, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed over a woman, and he stood up and walked in between her. (Bukhari 1332 and Abu Dawud 3188)"
"11664","(11664) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Ghalib or Abi Ghalib, on the authority of Anas, that a man’s funeral was brought and he stood up. He was at the head of the bed, and a woman’s funeral was brought. He stood at the bottom of that bed, and said: Al-Ala’ bin Ziyad, this is what you saw. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did it. He said: Yes, then he turned to us and said: Save it. (Tirmidhi 1034) Ahmad 3/118)"
"11665","(11645) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Mansour, who said: I said to Abu Rafi’: Where is Get up from the funeral. He said: So he took off his shoes, then said: Here, meaning in the middle."
"11666","(11666) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: I prayed behind Al-Hasan countless times at funerals for men and women. I did not see him caring where he got up from there."
"11667","(11667) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The one who prays at the funeral will stand up at Her chest"
"11668","(11668) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He stands from the woman around her breasts and from the man above. That"
"11669","(11669) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The woman is at her thighs and the man is at His chest while standing."
"11670","(11670) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Abu Husayn, who said: When Abdullah prayed over the funeral, he would stand Its middle and rises slightly above the woman’s chest."
"11671","(11671) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a man prays for The funeral took place at the chest."
"11672","(11672) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The one who performs the funeral prayer will stand at its chest."
"11673","(11673) Abbad bin Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of someone who heard Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: If the funeral of a man and a woman is The woman was brought and he placed her head at the man’s shoulders, then the imam stood at the woman’s head and in the middle of the man."
"11674","(11674) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, who said: I prayed with Wathili bin Al-Asqa’ at sixty funerals. Of the plague, men and women, and He placed them in two rows. He arranged the women in a row between the men’s hands, the head of the woman’s bed at my feet. Her companion, and the man’s head is at the feet of his companion’s bed."
"11675","(11675) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Habib Ibn Abi Thabit, who said: Sa’id Ibn Jubayr presented On the people of Mecca, they treat men and women equally when they pray over them, on their heads and feet. So he wanted them to place the woman’s head at the man’s waist."
"11676","(11676) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham: Concerning funerals, men and women, with their heads made equal, and Two rows between the Imam and the qiblah."
"11677","(11677) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail and Zechariah, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, as Ibrahim said."
"11678","(11678) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Dawud, he said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab say that."
"11679","(11679) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Musa, on the authority of Wathili bin Al-Asqa’, he said: It was He makes the heads of men to the knees of women."
"11680","(11680) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Miqdam, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The man is preferred. With the head"
"11681","(11681) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Hilal al-Mazini, who said: I saw Abu Hurairah Nine men and women will lead the prayer over his funeral, or seven, so he presented the women from those next to him, and made the men the color of the imam."
"11682","(11682) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that when men and women prayed over his funeral, He made the men among those that follow it, and the women behind that, among those that follow the qiblah."
"11683","(11683) Ibn Numair narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Uthman bin Abdullah bin Mawhib, that Zayd bin Thabit and Aba Huraira used to do that."
"11684","(11684) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, regarding the funerals of men and women. He said: The women should be in front of the men."
"11685","(11685) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ishmael and Zechariah, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, as Abraham said."
"11686","(11686) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Dawud, he said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab say that."
"11687","(11687) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: When Al-Harith prayed over the funerals of men and women, he made the men He colors him and gives precedence to women."
"11688","(11688) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ammar, a client of Banu Hashim, who said: Umm Kulthum and Zayd witnessed Ibn Omar, they died in one hour, so they took them out, and Sa’id Ibn Al-Aas prayed over them, so he made Zayd of what he had received, and he made Umm Kulthum in the hands of Zaid, and among the people on that day were people from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein. At the funeral"
"11689","(11689) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: When the funerals of men and women are gathered together, the men are made of He is next to the Imam, and the women are from those next to him, the free man and the slave. The kiss"
"11690","(11690) Hammad bin Masadi narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Rabbah bin Abi Rashid, who said: During the sweeping plague, people were praying. On the funerals of men and women separately, he said: Then Jabir bin Zayd came with what Abdul Rabbo thought, so he put the women in front of the men. So he prayed for them all."
"11691","(11691) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, that when he prayed over the funerals of men and women, he made the men From what follows, the Imam and the women behind that."
"11692","(11692) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, and Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Musa bin Talha, on the authority of Uthman, that He prayed over a man and a woman, and the man made of what followed them."
"11693","(11693) Ja`far ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Suleiman ibn Musa, on the authority of Wathili, who said: The plague occurred in the Levant and he died. Therein was much glad tidings, and he used to send blessings upon all the men and women, making the men among those next to him and the women among those next to him. The kiss"
"11694","(11694) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If the funerals of men and women come together, the men are made From what follows the imam, and women in front of that from what follows the qiblah."
"11695","(11695) Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Abdullah bin Umar prayed for Umm Kulthum bint Ali and her son Zaid. He said: So he made the boy from among those next to him, and the woman from among those next to the qiblah."
"11696","(11696) Abdullah bin Raja’ told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Salem and Al-Qasim. They said: The women are among those who follow the imam and the men. From what follows the qiblah."
"11697","(11697) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Men are in the hands of women."
"11698","(11698) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, he said: Muslim bin Mukhlid was in Egypt. He said: They came to us. With men and women, they were made to know not how they would do it, so Muslima said: Your ways in death are your ways in life. He said: So the women were made to follow the imam, and the men were in front of him."
"11699","(11699) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, that he prayed for men in a separate manner and for women. Ali alone, then he turned to the people and said: This is the one about which there is no doubt."
"11700","(11700) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he said regarding the funerals of men and women, he said: I was informed When Abu Al-Aswad disagreed over him, he prayed for those who struck him, and for those who struck him."
"11701","(11701) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: Al-Sha’bi prayed over the funeral of a boy and a man. He said: The man made of Layla, and the boy is in front of the man."
"11702","(11702) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, who said: I heard Al-Hasan say about the people lining up for the funeral. Then the man comes while they were waiting for him. He said: There is no problem."
"11703","(11703) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, he said: I see it, on the authority of Al-Qasim, that Omar waited for Ibn Umm Abd by praying for him. Utba bin Masoud."
"11704","(11704) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ziyad bin Jubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Mughirah Bin Shu'ba, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The child, may the blessings of God be upon him."
"11705","(11705) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, that Ibn Umar prayed over a miscarriage. Nafi’ said: I do not know whether he will live. Did he leave or died?"
"11706","(11706) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Bakr, he said: The most deserving of those upon whom We have prayed are our children."
"11707","(11707) Abdā narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: When his creation is completed and blown The spirit is in him, may peace be upon him."
"11708","(11708) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that He used to stand up for the soul of his child who had committed no sin, and say: Oh God, protect him from the torment of the grave."
"11709","(11709) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin; In the fall, if his character is made equal, he is named and blessings be upon him as one prays for the greatest."
"11710","(11710) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Jubayr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’ab. He said: The miscarriage is prayed for, and prayers are made for his parents for forgiveness and mercy. Yunus said: And the family of Ziyad raise him up. To the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I do not remember him."
"11711","(11711) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: We do not pray None of our children except that We prayed upon him."
"11712","(11712) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He prays for a minor as he prays for a The big one"
"11713","(11713) Muaz bin Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Pray for the fallen. And he named him, because he was born according to the natural disposition."
"11714","(11714) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: I asked Ibn Abi Layla, and he said: I realized what remained. The Ansar pray for one of their children."
"11715","(11715) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab; In a miscarriage, when he falls dead, he said: When the spirit is breathed into him, he will be prayed for, and that will be for four months."
"11716","(11716) Ahmad bin Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad narrated to us, saying: Asim Al-Ahwal narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Ahdab. He said: Ibn Umar was asked about praying for children, and he said: Because praying for one who has committed no sin is more beloved to me."
"11717","(11717) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim? He said: He will not pray for him until he prays."
"11718","(11718) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Hashim, on the authority of Ibrahim? He said: He will not pray for him until he prays."
"11719","(11719) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: I heard Saeed ibn Jubayr saying: The funeral prayer should not be prayed upon. The boy"
"11720","(11720) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: Jalas al-Shamiya narrated to us, saying: I heard Uthman bin Jahash, he said: I heard Samurah bin A grasshopper and his son died when he was young, so he said: Take him away and bury him, but do not pray over him, for there is no sin upon him. And pray to God for his parents to grant them abundance and reward, the like."
"11721","(11721) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, regarding a newborn who is not to be prayed for, nor is he even an inheritor. He deserves it"
"11722","(11722) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, that he asked them about the miscarriage. If he is dead, will the prayer be prayed over him? They said: No."
"11723","(11723) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, who said: He does not pray for the fallen, nor does he inherit it."
"11724","(11724) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: When it is recited, may the blessings of God be upon him. And he inherited, so if he did not perform it, the prayer was not prayed over him, and he was not inherited."
"11725","(11725) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a boy begins, the prayers are prayed upon him and he inherits, and if he does not... He deserves the blessings upon him, and he is not inherited."
"11726","(11726) Muaz bin Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The funeral prayer is not prayed upon him. It means falling."
"11727","(11727) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Rashid, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Al-Zubayr did not pray for his son. If he died young."
"11728","(11728) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab in The newborn, he said: He will not be inherited until it is completed."
"11729","(11729) Malik bin Ismail narrated to us, saying: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafali, he said: We were, and what we pray for the newborn."
"11730","(11730) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Suwayd, who said: We were, and we do not pray for newborns."
"11731","(11731) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The child of adultery is prayed for when he prays."
"11732","(11732) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Fudail ibn Ghazwan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he did not pray for a child. Adultery is minor or major."
"11733","(11733) Hafs told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to see the child of adultery on He dies in his bed in his house and his mother dies and he prays for them both."
"11734","(11734) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever prays over a funeral will get a qirat, and whoever waits until it is finished will get a qirat. Two carats. They said: What are two carats? He said: Like two great mountains. (Bukhari 1325. Muslim 652)"
"11735","(11735) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Adiy, on the authority of Zurr ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka’b, who said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever prays at a funeral gets a qirat, and whoever follows it until it is buried gets two qirats. A qirat is like Sunday (Ahmad 5/131, Ibn Majah 151)"
"11736","(11736) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, who said: I heard Al-Walid bin Abd al-Rahman narrating on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever prays over a funeral is entitled to a Qirat, and if he witnesses, he will bury it. It had two karats like Mount Uhud. Ibn Umar said: Watch what you say. He said: So they sent to Aisha, and she said he spoke the truth. (Ahmed 3)"
"11737","(11737) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Salim bin Abi al-Ja’d, on the authority of Ma’dan bin Abi Talha. Al-Amri, on the authority of Thawban, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever follows a funeral procession will get a reward, and whoever follows it will get a Qirat. Until it is buried, it has two qirats. They said: And the likeness of what is a qirat, O Messenger of God. He said: The smaller of them is like the size of Uhud.\n(Muslim 57. Ibn Majah 1540)"
"11738","(11738) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Salem al-Barrad, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, on the authority of Abdullah, they said: Whoever prays upon me A funeral has a qirat, and whoever bears witness until it is fulfilled has two qirats. A qirat is equivalent to one qirat."
"11739","(11739) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Jubayr bin Abi Salih, that he heard Abu Hurairah say Whoever prays at a funeral gets a qirat, and whoever witnesses it until it is finished gets two qirats, a qirat is the equivalent of one Uhud."
"11740","(11740) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, he said: Amr bin Yahya Al-Mazini narrated to me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yusuf bin Abdullah bin Salam, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever came to the funeral When he is with her family and walks with her until he prays over her, he gets a Qirat, and whoever witnesses her until she is buried gets two Qirats. Like someone. (Ahmed 27)"
"11741","(11741) Muhammad bin Bishr al-Abdi told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Salem al-Barrad, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever prays at a funeral gets a Qirat. (Ahmad 2/16)"
"11742","(11742) Al-Ala’ ibn Usaym narrated to us, saying: Abthar Abu Zubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Burd ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, he said: I heard Al-Bara’ bin Aazib saying, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever prays over a funeral will get a qirat. And whoever follows her until she is buried will have two Qirats. (Nasa’i 2067)"
"11743","(11743) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zaid, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No Muslim dies and a Muslim mother prays over him. They have not reached the age of being a hundred and interceding for him, but they have interceded for him. (Muslim 58. Ahmad 3/266)"
"11744","(11744) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Abu Bakkar, who said: I prayed with Abu Al-Malih at his funeral, and he said: : Straighten your ranks and improve your intercession. If I had been given the choice of a man, I would have chosen him. Abdullah bin bin Al-Salil told me, on the authority of some of the Prophet’s wives. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, Maimunah, who was her breast-brother. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no man A Muslim, whose nation may pray for him, unless they intercede on his behalf.\n Abu Al-Malih said: The mother is between forty and a hundred."
"11745","(11745) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Marthad bin Abdul Allah Al-Yazani, on the authority of Malik bin Hubaira Al-Shami, who had companions, said: Whenever a funeral was brought, he would say: With them, he divided them into rows of three, then he prayed over them, and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The rows were not lined up. Three Muslims are on the verge of death unless it becomes obligatory. (Tirmidhi 1028 and Abu Dawud 3158)"
"11746","(11746) Ismail bin Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Bukair bin Abi Al-Sumait narrated to us, saying: His qatadī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Al-Hasan, on the authority of Asas bin Salamah, he said: Whoever intercedes for forty things, their intercession will be accepted, and whoever witnesses for him ten, it will be accepted. Their testimony"
"11747","(11747) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Whoever has a hundred Muslims pray over him, he will be forgiven."
"11748","(11748) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman Abi Al-Yaqzan, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Jarir, who narrated it to us. He said: The lahud is ours and the hardship is ours. For others. (Ibn Majah 1555. Tabarani 2324)"
"11749","(11749) Hafs told us, on the authority of his father, who said: Lahad for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"11750","(11750) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: The grave of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his grave Bakr and Omar, then you bragged. (Ibn Saad 296)"
"11751","(11751) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was buried in Lahad."
"11752","(11752) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of the jurists of the people of Medina, who said: There were two men in Medina. They were digging graves. He said: One of them was making holes and the other was cutting. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died, they said: Whoever rose and was told to do the work he was doing, then the one who was blaspheming came up and they ordered him to commit blasphemy to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Ibn Saad 295)"
"11753","(11753) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, who said: The Prophet’s companions gathered May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, died, one man was blaspheming and the other was blaspheming, so they said: Oh God, let it go. To us, then the one who was an atheist came out and atheized him. (Ibn Majah 1428. Ahmed 8)"
"11754","(11754) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, Salim, and Al-Qasim. They said: It was the grave of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And Abu Bakr and Omar knelt down before him, and a brick was set up for them as a monument, and he made a punishment for them. (Ibn Saad 298)"
"11755","(11755) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The punishment of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, and to Abu Bakr and Omar."
"11756","(11756) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The punishment of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May peace and blessings be upon him."
"11757","(11757) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He hated making a hole in the grave and said, “It will be made in it.” To the end"
"11758","(11758) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, attacked him."
"11759","(11759) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of Al-Umari On the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, recommended that people be an atheist. (Ahmad 3/24, Ibn Saad 2)"
"11760","(11760) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, who said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’abi said, “Lahdna” to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"11761","(11761) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: We were with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace in his funeral, so we ended up at the grave, and he did not deny it."
"11762","(11762) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Az-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, He said: See which of them has the most collection of the Qur’an, so present it in the grave. (Tirmidhi 1016 and Abu Dawud 3129)"
"11763","(11763) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Abdul Rahman bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Ka'b bin Malik, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bring together two or three men in The grave (Bayhaqi 11)"
"11764","(11764) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, washed his body. Ali, Al-Fadl, and his names, and they took him into his grave, and Ali began to say: By my father, you and my mother are blessed alive and dead.\n He said: Ibn Abi Marhab narrated to us that Abd al-Rahman bin Awf entered the grave with them. He said: Al-Shu’abi said: Who is the guardian of the dead except His family? (Abu Dawud 3201 and Ibn Saad 277)"
"11765","(11765) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, that the one who was in charge of burying the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him, and his companions are four people, excluding the people: Ali, Al-Abbas, Al-Fadl, and Saleh, the client of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Hakim 362)"
"11766","(11766) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Enter the grave as much as you wish."
"11767","(11767) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Shafa’ or Witr will not harm you."
"11768","(11768) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Shafa’ or Witr will not harm you."
"11769","(11769) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm if a person enters the grave. Or a string."
"11770","(11770) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hafsah, who said: She advised Aisha, and she said: When the dust of my grave is leveled upon me So, while he was free, she wanted him to enter her grave, and Dhakwan had entered her grave while he was a slave."
"11771","(11771) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, who said: The grave is the closest one to it."
"11772","(11772) Hafs and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abza, He said: Zainab bint Jahsh died, and Omar said four times over her. Then he asked the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Who? Will he take her into her grave? They said: Who used to enter her life?"
"11773","(11773) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, saying: Ash’ath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A man enters his wife’s grave and will NS"
"11774","(11774) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of sheikhs from the Ansar who said: The Messenger came. May God bless him and grant him peace on the day of Uhud, Abdullah bin Amr bin Haram and Amr bin Al-Jamouh were killed, so he said: Bury them. In one grave, for they were pure in this world."
"11775","(11775) Shababi bin Siwar narrated to us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ka’b bin Malik, that Jabir bin Abdullah told him that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bring together the two men who had been killed. Someone is in one grave and he says: Which of the two of them has learned the Qur’an more? If it is pointed out to one of them, it means “in the grave.”\n(Bukhari 1343. Abu Dawud 3130)"
"11776","(11776) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It was disliked for two people to be buried in a grave. One"
"11777","(11777) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: See which of them has the most collection of the Qur’an, so they presented it in the grave."
"11778","(11778) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman bin Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ka'b bin Malik, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bring together two or three men in The grave"
"11779","(11779) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, that Abu Musa commanded that his grave be dug. To deepen his grave for him."
"11780","(11780) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Abdul Rahman, that Abu Musa recommended that the His grave"
"11781","(11781) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad that they both liked the grave to be deepened."
"11782","(11782) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad that they used to say, “The grave will be deepened.”"
"11783","(11783) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he said: The grave should be dug to the side."
"11784","(11784) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sulaym, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He instructed Omar to make the depth of his grave a full height. And spread it out"
"11785","(11785) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I witnessed the funeral of Al-Harith, so they spread a garment over his grave, and Abdul uncovered it. Allah bin Zaid said: He is only a man."
"11786","(11786) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Yahya bin Qays, that Shurayh recommended that they not spread anything over Ali. His grave is a garment."
"11787","(11787) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I witnessed the funeral of a man in which there was goodness, and Ibn Sirin, a garment was spread over his grave, He said: Al-Hasan, uncover him, for he is only a man, and Ibn Sirin did not see any harm in him."
"11788","(11788) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He entered Sa’d’s grave and spread a garment over him. (Abdul Razzaq 6477)"
"11789","(11789) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of his father, that he heard that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Nu’aym bin Masoud. Al-Ashja'i means the grave and removes the socket with his mouth, meaning the knot. (Ibn Saad 279)"
"11790","(11790) Hatim bin Wardan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: I witnessed Al-Ala’ bin Al-Hadrami, so we buried him, but we forgot to untie the knot, until we brought him into his grave. He said, “So we removed the milk from him, but we did not see him in the grave.” Something"
"11791","(11791) Abu Bakr ibn Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When the dead person is brought into the grave, it becomes permissible for him. All nodes."
"11792","(11792) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: The marriage contract is permissible on behalf of the dead."
"11793","(11793) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, who said: Al-Dahhak recommended it to me."
"11794","(11794) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, who said: It is permissible to perform the knot on behalf of the dead."
"11795","(11795) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, that he commanded that the knot be removed from him and that he be removed. His face is from the shroud."
"11796","(11796) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of al-Hasan and Muhammad that they hated having their shroud torn. The dead person when he enters the grave."
"11797","(11797) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Iyas bin Daghfal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Qais bin Abbad, on the authority of his father, that he bequeathed When you put me in my pit, cover the shroud behind my body until you take me to the ground."
"11798","(11798) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: I was with Anas at a funeral and he ordered the funeral of the deceased. So he was brought in by his feet."
"11799","(11799) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he brought in a dead person before His legs"
"11800","(11800) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: We witnessed the funeral of Ibn Maqil, and a man said: Your friend has recommended that you be entertained."
"11801","(11801) Ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to entertain you."
"11802","(11802) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: I told al-Sha’bi: A man buried a dead person, and he had washed him before. My feet are in the grave. He said: This, by God, is the Sunnah."
"11803","(11803) Abdah bin Sulaiman and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, that Qays made a will upon his death. To be asked smoothly."
"11804","(11804) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, that when he died His son commanded him and he was brought in by his feet."
"11805","(11805) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said, “I witnessed Abdullah bin Zayd enter Al-Harith from He kissed his feet and said: This is the Sunnah (Abu Dawud 3203, Bayhaqi 54)"
"11806","(11806) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Izzah, who said: I witnessed Ash-Sha’bi entering a dead person before. His legs"
"11807","(11807) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Until the death of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He was taken by the tribe and his grave was raised until he was known. (Abdul Razzaq 4671)"
"11808","(11808) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, who said: It was narrated on the authority of Umair bin Sa’id that Ali brought a dead person From before."
"11809","(11809) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: It is taken from The kiss"
"11810","(11810) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Ata’, the client of Banu Asad, who said: I witnessed the death of Ibn Abbas. His guardian was Ibn al-Hanafiyyah. He said: He said the takbir to him four times and brought him in from the front."
"11811","(11811) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Umair bin Saeed, that Ali said “Allahu Akbar” to Ali. Yazid ibn al-Mukaffaf took four days and brought him in from the tribe."
"11812","(11812) Ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Al-Manhal ibn Khalifa, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He took him from the direction of the qiblah, and he recited the “Allahu Akbar” four times, meaning the dead. (Tirmidhi 1057)"
"11813","(11813) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubad Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he brought in a dead person by the tribe."
"11814","(11814) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, with something similar."
"11815","(11815) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: When you place your dead in their graves, say: In the name of God and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted you. (Abu Dawud 3205. Ahmad 2/27)"
"11816","(11816) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to say That"
"11817","(11817) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was When the dead person is placed in the grave, he greets him and says: In the name of God, by God, and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of God.\n(Tirmidhi 1046 and Ibn Majah 1550)"
"11818","(11818) Sharik and Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Mudrik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Omar, that he used to say When the dead person was placed in his grave, and Abu Al-Ahwas said when he settled on him, O God, grant him his money, his family, and his clan. And the sin is great, so forgive him."
"11819","(11819) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Khaythāmī, he said: They used to prefer it when they were given The dead in the grave are to say: In the name of God and in the path of God and upon the religion of the Messenger of God, O God, protect him from the torment of the grave. And the torment of the Fire, and from the evil of Satan."
"11820","(11820) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, that he used to say: In the name of God and in the path of O God, O God, make his grave spacious for him, and enlighten him in it, and join him to his Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and you He is satisfied, not angry."
"11821","(11821) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, who said: If you place the dead In the grave, say: In the name of God, and to God, and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"11822","(11822) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: When you place the dead person in the grave, say: In the name of God. And upon the family of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"11823","(11823) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas, that he buried a son of his, and he said: Oh God, dry the earth beside him. And open the gates of heaven for his soul, and replace his home with a better home."
"11824","(11824) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, who said: When the dead person is placed in the grave, do not say: In the name of God, but say in the way of God and according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and according to the religion of Abraham, upright A Muslim, and he was not of the polytheists. O God, make him steadfast with firm words in the Hereafter. O God, make him better than he was. Concerning him, O God, do not deprive us of his reward, and do not test us after him. He said: And these verses were revealed about the companion of the grave: {He establishes Allah is the one who believes in the firm word in this life and in the hereafter}"
"11825","(11825) Saal bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I said to Muhammad, “If I put the dead body in the grave, what should I say?” He said: Nothing."
"11826","(11826) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, he said: It was Ali He says when he dreams when he sleeps, “In the name of God and in the way of God, and upon the religion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And he says when The man entered the grave."
"11827","(11827) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Abi Bakr, who said: When Anas Ibn Malik made a settlement with Ali The dead person is in his grave. He rose up to him and said: Oh God, return your servant to you, be kind to him and have mercy on him. Oh God, dry the earth beside him. And open the gates of heaven to his soul, and accept it from you with good acceptance. O God, if he is a doer of good, double his benevolence to him, or he said: Increase his goodness, and if he is offensive, then forgive him."
"11828","(11828) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Umair bin Saeed, that Ali said the takbeer to Yazid four times, and he said: Oh God, your servant and the son of your servant have descended upon you today, and you are the best to descend upon him. Oh God, expand his entrance for him, and forgive him. His sin, for we only know what is good, and you know it best."
"11829","(11829) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Mulki, who said when he finished the grave of Abdullah bin Al-Sa'ib Ibn Abbas stood at the grave, stood over it, then prayed, then left."
"11830","(11830) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Shayban, on the authority of Khaled ibn Samir, he said: I was with Al-Ahnaf in At his funeral, Al-Ahnaf sat and I sat with him. When he finished burying her - Dirar ibn Al-Qaqa’ Al-Tamimi - I saw Al-Ahnaf come to the funeral. On his grave, he stood up and began to say the two before the supplication, and said: By God, I did not know such-and-such. By God, I did not know such-and-such. Then he supplicated for him."
"11831","(11831) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Umair bin Saeed, who said: I prayed with Ali over Yazid bin Al-Mukaffaf said the takbir on him four times, then he walked until he came to him and said: Oh God, your servant and the son of your servant have descended upon you today. So forgive him his sins, and make his path easy for him, for we only know what is good, and you know it best."
"11832","(11832) Ibn Aliyah told us, he said: I saw Ayoub standing at the grave and praying for the dead. He said: And perhaps I saw him. He prays for him while he is in the grave before he comes out."
"11833","(11833) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Umair bin Saeed, that Ali was buried in the grave of Ibn Al-Mukaffaf."
"11834","(11834) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Umair bin Sa’id, that Ali was buried in the grave of Ibn The blind person"
"11835","(11835) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Zaid, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He was buried in his grave."
"11836","(11836) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, he said: Aamir bin Jushayb and others from the Levant narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Darda'i said: Part of the full reward for a funeral is to dig in the grave."
"11837","(11837) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ya`qub al-Ahlafi, who said: Inform me of someone who saw Zayd ibn Arqam attacking He buried three."
"11838","(11838) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of his uncle: that Ali was buried in his grave."
"11839","(11839) Dawud narrated to us on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If you wish, search in the grave, and if you wish, do not dig in it."
"11840","(11840) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, that he saw Salem bin Abdullah on the verge of a grave. Then he left and did not put any dirt in it."
"11841","(11841) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Na’am, who said: A man from Jenin narrated to me. He said: I was with Abu Hurairah at a funeral and he buried me in his grave."
"11842","Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman Baqi bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr Abd told us Allah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shayba, said:\n(11842) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Maimun bin Mihran, that he commanded that The dirt is covered abundantly."
"11843","(11843) Othman bin Ali told us, on the authority of Asim bin Badla, who said: I witnessed Omar bin Abdul Aziz when a tooth was buried on him. The dirt is old."
"11844","(11844) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Quran. He said: Abu Karb, or Abu Harb, narrated to me on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that he narrated to him, that his father advised him, he said: When you put me in the grave, I will be like the dust."
"11845","(11845) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Othman bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made She has a ton of reeds."
"11846","(11846) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Amr bin Sharhabeel, He said: Throw tons of reeds on me, for I saw the immigrants preferring it over everything else."
"11847","(11847) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he hated to put anything in the grave except milk. Clean, he said: He hated brickwork, and he said: If they do not find brick, then reed."
"11848","(11848) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Misra, that he commanded, he said: Make There are tons of reeds on my grave."
"11849","(11849) Quraysh bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he saw no harm in teak and reed, and he hated it. Al-Ajar, meaning in the grave."
"11850","(11850) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Isa, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, he said The brick was erected on the grave of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ibn Saad 297)"
"11851","(11851) Mu’ttam bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: If you wish, you can build the grave as a builder, and if you wish I set up the brick as a monument."
"11852","(11852) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein that the grave of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace They set up a monument over him, peace and blessings be upon him."
"11853","(11853) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, Salim, and Al-Qasim. They said: It was the grave of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And Abu Bakr and Omar knelt down before him, and a monument was set up for them."
"11854","(11854) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, Salim, and Al-Qasim. They said: It was the grave of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And Abu Bakr and Omar kneeled before him."
"11855","(11855) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: I saw the graves of martyrs with bodies growing on them."
"11856","(11856) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Sufyan al-Tamar, who said: I entered the house in which was the grave of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, and I saw the grave of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the graves of Abu Bakr and Omar, with a pillar. (Bukhari 1390)"
"11857","(11857) Al-Ashja’i narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Abu Na’am, who said: I testified with Musa bin Talha. A funeral, and he said: Jamharwa, Jamharwa, meaning Sunmo."
"11858","(11858) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I saw the graves of martyrs One of them prostrated himself."
"11859","(11859) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of a man, who said: I saw the grave of Ibn Umar after He was buried a few days later."
"11860","(11860) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Muhammad, that he disliked having the grave marked."
"11861","(11861) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaym bin Hayyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They hated that he should know. The man is his grave."
"11862","(11862) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, on the authority of Kathir ibn Zaid, on the authority of al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, he said: When Othman bin Mazun died, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, buried him in Al-Baqi’, and he said to a man, “Go to that rock.” So bring it to me so that I may place it by his grave so that I may make it known to him. (Abu Dawud 3198)"
"11863","(11863) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of al-Qasim, that he commanded, saying: O my son, do not write against me. My grave, and do not honor it except to the extent that it repels the water from me."
"11864","(11864) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade He granted that it be built upon, and Suleiman bin Musa said, on the authority of Jabir, and that it be written upon. (Abu Dawud 3217, Tirmidhi 1052)"
"11865","(11865) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked the tablet being placed on the grave."
"11866","(11866) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked making a mosque over the grave."
"11867","(11867) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, Lahad said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him, and his grave was raised so that he would be known."
"11868","(11868) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw the grave of Othman bin Maz'un is high."
"11869","(11869) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Ibrahim bin Ata bin Abi Maimun told us, on the authority of his father, that Imran bin Husayn recommended that they make his grave square, and that they raise him four fingers high, or something like that."
"11870","(11870) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Mihran, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he commanded that they not put a tent over his grave."
"11871","(11871) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Mujma’, on the authority of his paternal aunt Umm al-Numan, on the authority of the daughter of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri, that Abu Saeed said: Do not set up a tent over my grave."
"11872","(11872) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Ata, who said: I witnessed the death of Ibn Abbas, and his guardian was Ibn al-Hanafi. He built a building on it for three days."
"11873","(11873) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, that Omar laid a tent over Zainab’s grave."
"11874","(11874) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Tha’labya, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ka’b say: These are the rugs that are on The graves are newly created."
"11875","(11875) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He was placed in the grave of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He handed over a piece of red velvet that he had collected on the day of Khaybar. He said: They made it because Medina is a marshy land."
"11876","(11876) Ghandar and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Jamra, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that it was placed in the grave of the Messenger of God. May God bless him and grant him peace. Red cotton. (Muslim 91. Ahmad 1/355)"
"11877","(11877) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, that Lahad said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Shaqran was thrown into the His grave is a piece of velvet that he used to ride with during his life. (Tirmidhi 1047 and Abd al-Razzaq 6387)"
"11878","(11878) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Sulaym, on the authority of Umair bin Sa`id, that Ali rose over a grave until he was buried. And he said: Let one of you stand over his grave until he is buried."
"11879","(11879) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qais, who said: I witnessed Alqamiya, he rose over the dead until he was buried."
"11880","(11880) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Thumamah, he said: We went out with Fadalah bin Ubaid to The land of the Romans. He said: He was a worker for Mu’awiyah on the road, and a cousin of ours, called Nafi’, was injured, so may his blessings be upon him. He stood in his pit until he saw him."
"11881","(11881) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Ubaid bin Umayr, he said: Abdullah was When Ibn al-Zubayr died, he would not remain standing until he buried him."
"11882","(11882) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abi Qalabab, he said: By God, Their standing on the grave is an innovation until they are placed in their grave when the prayer is prayed over them."
"11883","(11883) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I asked Al-Sha’bi about standing up for the funeral until it is placed in the grave. He said: I did not see anyone doing that except Abu Marhoum, that Syrian, and they used to mock him."
"11884","(11884) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked standing when The grave"
"11885","(11885) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: It was mentioned to Al-Sha’biyyah to stand up for the funeral until it is laid out. It was as if he did not know that. He said: So I mentioned that to Mujahid. He said: If he prays upon her, he does not sit. Until you are placed."
"11886","(11886) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade He granted permission to plaster the grave, to sit on it, and to build on it."
"11887","(11887) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit bin Zaid, who said: Hamada narrated to me, on the authority of Anisa bint Zaid. Ibn Arqam, she said: Ibn Lazaid, called Suwayd, died, and a boy of his, or a maid, bought plaster and bricks, and he said to him: Zaid: What do you want to do with this? He said: I wanted to build his grave and plaster it. He said: You have despised and pecked, do not bring him anything near. Fire touched him."
"11888","(11888) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Saleh, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Ezzah, who said: I heard him say: Regarding plastering the grave, he said: Do not plaster it."
"11889","(11889) Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Khaythami, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafli, who said: If I die, then Do not call anyone to Me, and do not bring me any plaster, brick, or stick, and let no woman accompany me."
"11890","(11890) Hushaym narrated to us, Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Abraham, that he used to hate the wage."
"11891","(11891) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to pay rent in Their graves"
"11892","(11892) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to love milk but dislike it. They like bricks, they like reeds, and they dislike wood."
"11893","(11893) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, who said: I was walking with Abdullah in The coward, so he said: To step on hot coals until they are extinguished is more beloved to me than to step on a grave."
"11894","(11894) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Bakra, who said: Because It is more beloved to me to step on a coal until it is extinguished than to step on a grave."
"11895","(11895) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Salem Abi Abdullah al-Barrad, who said: I heard Ibn Masoud He says that stepping on hot coals is more beloved to me than stepping on the grave of a Muslim man."
"11896","(11896) Shababi told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid, that Abu Al-Khair informed him that Uqba bin Amir He said: To step on hot coals, or on the edge of a sword until my feet are snatched away is more beloved to me than to walk on the grave of a Muslim man. And I do not care whether I relieved myself in graves or in the market place while people were watching."
"11897","(11897) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad that they both hated sitting on it and walking. Aliyah"
"11898","(11898) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala bin Al-Shakhir, he said: So-and-so, you are walking. On your graves? I said: Yes. He said: How does it rain?"
"11899","(11899) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of his father, he said: I was following Abu He saw it at funerals, and he used to search the graves. He said: Because one of you sits on hot coals and his clothes are burned, then His shirt, then his lower garment until it reaches his skin is dearer to me than sitting on a grave. (Muslim 961 Abu Dawud 3220)"
"11900","(11900) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, that he hated sitting on graves or walking. Aliyah"
"11901","(11901) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade He said hello to sit on it."
"11902","(11902) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no middle ground. A graveyard, and he does not urinate in it."
"11903","(11903) Shababi told us, on the authority of Laith bin Saad, on the authority of Yazid, that Abu Al-Khair informed him that Uqba bin Amir He said: I do not care in graves, relieving myself, or in the market while people are watching."
"11904","(11904) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Zazan, He said: Whenever Ali entered the cemetery, he would say: Peace be upon the believers and Muslims in these lands. You are very special to us. We are your followers, and we will follow you, for indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we shall return."
"11905","(11905) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Jundub Al-Azdi, he said: We went out with Salman went into confusion until when we reached the graves, he turned to his right and said: Peace be upon you, O people of the land. Believing men and believing women, you are close to us and we are your followers, and indeed we will return to your tracks."
"11906","(11906) Jarir bin Abdul-Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Khaythami and Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid because they used to greet the graves."
"11907","(11907) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I do not know of any harm for a man to visit the grave. Then he greets him."
"11908","(11908) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, that he saw Salim bin Abdullah not He passes by night, and there is no day in a grave without greeting him, and we are traveling with him. He says, “Peace be upon you,” so I said to him about that. So he told me, on the authority of his father, that he used to do that."
"11909","(11909) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Sulayman bin Buraidah, on the authority of His father, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to teach them when they went out to the cemeteries, and their speaker used to say: Peace be upon you, O people of this land, among the believers and Muslims, and indeed, God willing, we will be among those who will follow you. You are our superior. We are your followers, and we ask God to grant us and you well-being. (Abu Dawud 3230; Ahmad 353)"
"11910","(11910) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of Aamir ibn Saad, on the authority of his father, that He would return from his village and pass by the graves of the martyrs and say: Peace be upon you, and indeed we will follow you. Then he would say: To his companions: Don’t you greet the martyrs and they will respond to you?"
"11911","(11911) Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin al-Hasan al-Jari, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saad al-Jari, he said: He said: According to Abu Hurairah, O Abdullah, if you pass by graves and you know them, say: Peace be upon you, companions of the graves. You pass by graves and do not recognize them, so say: Peace be upon the Muslims."
"11912","(11912) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, Al-Hakam bin Fasil narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Ubaid bin Jubayr, on the authority of Abu Muwaybah, the client of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was ordered to He goes out to Al-Baqi' and prays for them, or greets them. (Ahmad 3/489, Darami 78)"
"11913","(11913) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, that he was asked about greeting the graves, and he said: It was not Their work"
"11914","(11914) Khalid bin Al-Harith narrated to us, saying: Hisham was asked: Did Urwa come to the grave of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? So he greets him? He said: No."
"11915","(11915) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that if he wanted to go out, he would enter He entered the mosque and prayed, then he came to the grave of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of God, peace be upon you. Abu Bakr, peace be upon you, my father. Then his face would be, and when he came from a journey he would come to the mosque, and he would do that before He enters her house."
"11916","(11916) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Thumamah bin Shafi, who said: We went out on a campaign during the time of Mu’awiyah. To this path, and upon us is Fadalah bin Ubaid. He said, “The son of a cousin of mine, called Nafi’, died, so Fadalah Ali rose up with us.” It was dug, and when we buried it, he said: Lighten up on its hole, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had ordered it to be leveled. Graves\n(Ahmad 6/18, Bayhaqi 411)"
"11917","(11917) Zayd bin Harun told us, Sulaiman bin Kathir informed us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharhabeel, that Othman came out and ordered the graves to be leveled, so they were leveled except for the grave of Umm Amr, Othman’s son, so he said: What is this? The grave. They said: The grave of Umm Amr, so he ordered it to be leveled."
"11918","(11918) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Ash’u, on the authority of Hanash al-Kinani, who said: A companion of Ali entered upon me. Then he said: Go, and do not leave any stone without throwing it, nor any grave without leveling it. Then he called him and said: Do you know where? Where did I send you? I sent you to do what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to do. (Abu Dawud 3210, Ahmad 1/145)"
"11919","(11919) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Fazara, on the authority of a servant of Ibn Abbas, who said: Ibn Abbas said to me, “When I see the people They buried a dead person, so they created in his grave what is not in the graves of Muslims, so they made it with the graves of Muslims."
"11920","(11920) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Leveling graves is part of the Sunnah."
"11921","(11921) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, similar to him."
"11922","(11922) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Mansour bin Abdul Rahman, who said: A man said to Al-Sha’bi: A man buried a dead person and leveled it. His grave was in the ground, and he said: I came to the graves of the martyrs of Uhud, and behold, they were marked out of the ground."
"11923","(11923) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad Ibn Sirin was asked: Are graves covered? He said: I don't know of any harm in it."
"11924","(11924) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked paving over graves."
"11925","(11925) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol, that he hated it."
"11926","(11926) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I forbade you from visiting graves, so visit them. (Abu Dawud 3227)"
"11927","(11927) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Amr bin Amir, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade visiting graves, then he said: Visit them, and do not say “forsaken.”\n(Ahmad 3/250, Hakim 376)"
"11928","(11928) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd, on the authority of Rabi’ah bin Al-Nabighi, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade visiting graves, then he said: I was I forbid you from visiting graves, so visit them and you will be reminded of the Hereafter. (Ahmad 1/1451 Abu Ali 278)"
"11929","(11929) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, saying: Zaid bin Kaysan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited his mother’s grave and wept, and those around him cried, so he said: I asked for permission. My Lord, I ask forgiveness for her, but he did not give me permission. I asked him for permission to visit her grave, so he gave me permission, so visit the graves. For it reminds you of death.\n(Muslim 1088, Ahmad 2/441)"
"11930","(11930) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Buraidah, On the authority of his father, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, conquered Mecca, he came to a grave, and he sat next to him and made The addressee sat down, and the people sat around him, so he stood up and wept, and Omar, who was one of the boldest of people, met him and said: By my father and my mother, O Messenger of God, what made you cry? He said: This is my mother’s grave. I asked my Lord to visit him, and he gave me permission. I asked him to ask for forgiveness, but he did not give me permission. So I mentioned it, and my soul became sad and wept. He said, “He did not see it.” And that was more. Weeping about it that day. (Ahmad 355. Ibn Hibban 5390)"
"11931","(11931) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, Farqad al-Sabkhi narrated to us, Jabir bin Yazid narrated to us, Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I have forbidden you from visiting graves, and Muhammad was given permission to visit his mother’s grave, so visit her and she will remember you. (Daraqutni 69. Abd al-Razzaq 6714)"
"11932","(11932) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Asama bin Zayd, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Asim bin Umar died, and Ibn Umar is absent. When he came, he said, “Show me to his grave,” and he stood over it and made supplication."
"11933","(11933) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Malika, who said: Abdul died Al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr in Al-Habashi, Ibn Juraij Al-Habashi said, twelve miles from Mecca, so he was buried in Mecca. When Aisha came to his grave and said:\nAnd we were like two liars for a long time until it was said, “They will never break.”\nWhen we separated, it was as if Malik and I had been together for a long time and had not spent the night together.\n Then she said: By God, if I had attended you, I would have buried you where you died, and if I had witnessed you, I would not have visited you."
"11934","(11934) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that when he came and died Some of his children, and he said: Show me his grave, and they will show him to it, and he will go and stand over him and pray for him."
"11935","(11935) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Abu Farwa Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Suba’, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of his father, said: I sat with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in a gathering, and I saw him sad, so he said to him: A man from the people: What is the matter with you, O Messenger of God, as if you are sad? He said: I mentioned my mother, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: I forbade you from sacrificial meat. You may eat it except for three days, then eat and be fed and save what you wish, and I have forbidden you from visiting graves. He wanted to visit his mother’s grave, so let him visit it, and your prohibition was regarding the tambourine, the hantam, the saddlebags, and the naqir, so avoid them. Every intoxicant, and abstain from what pleases you."
"11936","(11936) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jahadi, who said: I heard Abu Salih narrating after On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed women who visit graves and those who stay in mosques over them. And the lamps."
"11937","(11937) Abdul bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, that Umm Salama mentioned to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He saw a church in the land of Abyssinia. It is called Maria. She mentioned to him what she had seen. There are some pictures in it, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Those are a people who, when a righteous servant, or a righteous man, dies among them. They built a mosque over his grave and made those pictures in it. Those are the worst of creation in the sight of God Almighty. (Bukhari 434, Muslim 375)"
"11938","(11938) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He says: Among the worst people are those whom the Hour will overtake while they are alive, and those who take graves as places of worship. (Ibn Khuzaymah 789. Ahmad 1/405)"
"11939","(11939) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, that he disliked visiting the grave and praying. With him"
"11940","(11940) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of Hassan bin Hassan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Do not take my grave as a place of rest, nor take your homes as graves, but pray for me wherever you are, for your prayer is You inform me."
"11941","(11941) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Zaid bin Aslam, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God’s peace and blessings be upon him: O God, do not make my grave an idol to be prayed to. God’s wrath is intense against a people who have taken the graves of their prophets. Mosques"
"11942","(11942) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has cursed people who take the graves of their prophets as places of worship."
"11943","(11943) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: Omar said: Because we do not find anyone more astray. From the visitor of the grave."
"11944","(11944) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They hated visiting him. Graves"
"11945","(11945) Qubaisa narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Bahman, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Hassan bin Thabit, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cursed women who visit graves. (Ahmad 442)"
"11946","(11946) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Had it not been that the Messenger of God had prayed May God bless him and grant him peace. He forbade visiting graves. I would visit your daughter’s grave."
"11947","(11947) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Yunus al-Baili, who said: I heard a sheikh in Mecca who was originally A Roman narrated on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: A man was circumambulating the Kaaba, saying, “Awha, awha.” Abu Dharr said: A woman came out One night, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in the graveyard, burying that man, and he had a lamp with him. (Abu Dawud 3156)"
"11948","(11948) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Hassan bin Muhammad, that Fatima was buried at night."
"11949","(11949) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, that Ali was buried So he fasted at night."
"11950","(11950) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father, who said: I was with Uqba bin Amir, and he was asked about Takbir for the dead. He said: Four. I said: Night and day are the same. He said: Night and day are the same. I said: The dead are buried. At night, he said: Abu Bakr was buried at night."
"11951","(11951) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Al-Walid Ibn Abi Hisham, on the authority of Al-Qasim Ibn Muhammad, Abu Bakr was buried. At night"
"11952","(11952) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his followers, that Ibn Masoud was buried at night. He said: And his followers were He hates that."
"11953","(11953) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ismail ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn al-Subaq, that Umar buried Abu Bakr. at night, then he entered the mosque and prayed the Witr prayer with three strings."
"11954","(11954) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Shurayh, that he used to bury some of his sons at night. Hate crowding."
"11955","(11955) Khalid al-Zayat told us, on the authority of Zur’a ibn Amr, a servant of the Hubab family, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amr, who said: We buried Uthman Ibn Affan, after the last night’s dinner in Al-Baqi’, he said, “I was the fourth of four among those who carried him.”"
"11956","(11956) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Abu Bakr died on the night of On Tuesday, he was buried on the night of Tuesday."
"11957","(11957) Ghandar and Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, that He saw no harm in burying at night."
"11958","(11958) Al-Fadl ibn Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Shayban, on the authority of Khaled ibn Samir Al-Sadusi, he said: I asked Anas about Praying for the dead at night, and he said: Praying for the dead at night is nothing but the same as praying for the dead during the day."
"11959","(11959) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Abraham was buried at night and we were afraid."
"11960","(11960) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurra, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he disliked being buried at night."
"11961","(11961) Abdul bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Fatima bint Muhammad, on the authority of Amriya, on the authority of Aisha She said: We did not know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had been buried until we heard the sound of sweepers at the end of the night, the night of Wednesday. Muhammad said, “And the surveyors of passage.” (Ahmad 62. Ibn Rahawi 993)"
"11962","(11962) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Ali said: When Abu Talib died, I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Peace and blessings of God be upon him. I said, O Messenger of God, that your misguided uncle has died. So he said to me: Go and bury him, and do not talk to anything until You will come to me, he said, so I went off and saw him, then I returned to him with traces of dirt and dust on me, so he prayed for me with some invitations. I am pleased that I have in it everything that is on earth."
"11963","(11963) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Najiya, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said something similar, and he said, “Then command me to wash.”"
"11964","(11964) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: Umm al-Harith ibn Abi Rabi’i died while... Christianity, so the companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, bore witness to it."
"11965","(11965) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Umm Al-Harith died and she was a Christian, so her companions gave her witnesses. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"11966","(11966) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Ismail, on the authority of Aamir bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said she died My mother is a Christian, so she went to Omar and mentioned that to him, and he said: Get on your animal and walk in front of her."
"11967","(11967) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: The mother of a man from Thaqif died while she was a Christian, so he asked Ibn Maqil, and he said “I would like to accompany her, but not follow her.” He said, “Get on a mount and walk in front of her at a distance, for if you walk in front of her, you will not With her"
"11968","(11968) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, who said: I heard Ibn Umar, he was asked about the Muslim man. He follows his Christian mother when she dies. He said: He follows her and walks in front of her."
"11969","(11969) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Dirar ibn Murra, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, who said: A Christian man died He had a son, Muslim, but he did not follow him, so he said: Ibn Abbas should have followed him, buried him, and asked forgiveness for him. In her life"
"11970","(11970) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: When Abu Talib died, Ali came to the Prophet and prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Your uncle, the infidel sheikh, has died, and what do you think of him? He said: I think that you should wash him and bathe him, and he commanded him. By washing."
"11971","(11971) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Dirar ibn Murra, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, who said: A Christian man died. So his son entrusted him to the people of his religion, and this was mentioned to Ibn Abbas, and he said: It would not be upon him if he had walked with him and made him mad. And he asked forgiveness for him while he was alive, then he recited: {And Abraham’s seeking forgiveness for his father was not} the verse."
"11972","(11972) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man dies at sea, he is placed in a zabeel, then He was thrown away"
"11973","(11973) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning the one who dies at sea, he said: He should be washed, shrouded, mummified, and prayers should be prayed over him, then his feet should be tied. Something, then he throws it into the sea."
"11974","(11974) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, who said: I went out with Salem bin Abdullah at a funeral. So he took a different path and opposed her. When he reached the grave, he sat down before she was placed."
"11975","(11975) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Shurayh and Zayd ibn Arqam used to take things by another means. The funeral"
"11976","(11976) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: He advised Urwah not to be buried in Al-Baqi’, and he said: If he is a believer, I do not like to be subjected to hardship, but if he is an immoral person, I do not like to be oppressed by him."
"11977","(11977) Malik bin Ismail narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, said: Bury me in the grave of Uthman bin Mad’un."
"11978","(11978) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, that Khaythami recommended that he be buried in a grave. The poor of his people."
"11979","(11979) Abu Asama told us, Ismail bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Qais, he said: Aisha said when she attended her Death: Bury me with the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for I was born after him."
"11980","(11980) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, that Umar said to Abdullah ibn Umar, “Go to Aisha, so say hello and say: Omar ibn al-Khattab asks permission to be buried with his companion, so Abdullah came to her and found her sitting. He cried and said hello, then he said: Omar ibn al-Khattab asks permission to be buried with his two companions, and she said, “I have been, and by God, I want him to be.” For myself, and I would not prefer it today to myself."
"11981","(11981) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I asked him about a woman who dies. On her breath of immorality, he prayed for her and said: Bless the one who says there is no god but Allah."
"11982","(11982) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amr ibn Yahya, on the authority of Abu al-Nu’man, that the Messenger of God prayed May God bless him and grant him peace upon the child of the adulterer and upon the mother who died in childbirth."
"11983","(11983) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, who said: I said to my father in front of him: A man drinks alcohol and dies. He prayed for him, he said, yes, perhaps he lay down on his bed once and said: There is no god but Allah, so he was forgiven for it."
"11984","(11984) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said, “Blessings be upon the one who killed himself and upon the souls.” From adultery, and the one who dies must drink alcohol."
"11985","(11985) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan Al-Sarraj, who said: Abu Wael prayed for a woman who died, and I said to him: She is being irritated, so he said: Yes, pray for the one who prays towards the qiblah."
"11986","(11986) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Bless the one who prays towards your qiblah."
"11987","(11987) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I do not know that any of the people of knowledge Nor did the Followers abandon the prayer over any of the people of the tribe out of sin."
"11988","(11988) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I said to Al-Hasan that I had a neighbor from the Kharijites who died. What is his funeral? He said: Did he attack the Muslims? He said: I said, “No.” He said, “Then attend his funeral, for the action is more important to him than the opinion.”"
"11989","(11989) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, that a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He was wounded and hurt him, so he crawled to the horn of his sword and took a pair of scissors and killed himself with it, so the Prophet did not pray. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and Sharik mentioned, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, he said: I only leave the prayers upon him out of politeness to him.\n(Muslim 1077, Abu Dawud 3177)"
"11990","(11990) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Imran, who said: I asked Ibrahim al-Nakha’i about a man who killed Should he pray for himself? He said: Yes, prayer is a Sunnah."
"11991","(11991) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of his companions, on the authority of Abraham, in captivity, being taken captive from the enemy’s land, and he said: Then He affirmed monotheism and the two testimonies, may peace and blessings be upon him."
"11992","(11992) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Khaythamiyah, he said: When he prayed once, he prayed upon him."
"11993","(11993) Jarir told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If he says: There is no god but Allah, may the blessings of God be upon him."
"11994","(11994) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jabr, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: He was a young man. A Jew serving the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he fell ill, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to him to bring him back and said: Do I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that I am the Messenger of Allah? He said: So he started to look at his father and said: Say as Muhammad says to you. He said: Then he died, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Pray for your companion (Hakim 363, Bukhari 5452, Ahmad 3/260)"
"11995","(11995) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sahl al-Siraj, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin being asked about a people who came Because of captivity, so when they ordered them to pray, they prayed, and if they did not command them, they did not pray, and a man among them died, so he said: It has become clear. Indeed, he is one of the inmates of Hell. They said: No, as has become clear to us. He said: Wash him, shroud him, embalm him, and pray over him."
"11996","(11996) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Shaqri, who said: A man at Al-Shaabi said, “I bring slaves and some of them die. Should I pray for them?” He said: “If he prays, pray for him, and if he does not pray, then do not pray.” Aliyah"
"11997","(11997) Hammad bin Abi Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: When an unbeliever wanders while in the market May peace be upon him."
"11998","(11998) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Asbaani, who said: Abu Salih came to me to console me, on the authority of a son of mine, So he started narrating on the authority of Abu Sa`id and Abu Hurairah. The women said to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “Make a day for us as you have made for the men.” He said: So he came to the women. So he exhorted them, taught them, and commanded them, and said to them: There is no woman who buries three people except that they will protect her from the Fire. He said: Then a woman said: O Messenger of God, I presented two. He said: Three, then he said: Two and two. Abu Hurairah said: Whoever has not yet reached the age of breaking oath. (Bukhari 1020, Muslim 153)"
"11999","(11999) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: Who He presented three of his sons. He will not enter Hell unless he fulfills his oath. (Bukhari 1251, Muslim 2028)"
"12000","(12000) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Talq bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: She came The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave a woman a son, and she said: O Messenger of God, pray to God for him, for I have buried three. He said: Did you bury three people? She said: Yes, he said: I was severely protected from the fire. (Bukhari 1471, Muslim 156)"
"12001","(12001) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, Abdullah bin Qais narrated to us, he said: I was One night with Abu Burdah, Al-Harith bin Uqish entered and Al-Harith told us that night that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: There is no Muslim who dies for four transgressions except that God admits them to Paradise. They said: O Messenger God and three. He said: And three. They said: O Messenger of God and two. He said: And two. (Ibn Majah 4323. Ahmad 4/212)"
"12002","(12002) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Abu Ramla, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Muslim, on the authority of Muadh ibn Jabal, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: He made obligatory the one of three. They said: And the one of two, O Messenger of God. He said: And the two (Ibn Majah 1609. Ahmad 5/237)"
"12003","(12003) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd, al-Qasim narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. There is no believer who dies having three children who have not reached the age of breaking oaths except that God admits them to them. Heaven, thanks to His mercy towards them. (Ahmad 4/386)"
"12004","(12004) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, Othman bin Hakim narrated to us, on the authority of Amr Al-Ansari, on the authority of Umm Sulaym ibn Malhan Umm Anas said that she heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: There are no Muslims who will die for three of them. Children who have not reached the age of breaking oaths except that God admits them to Paradise thanks to His mercy. (Ahmad 6/376, Tabarani 306)"
"12005","(12005) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Musa Al-Janni, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Whoever offers three He was born patient and seeking reward. They shielded him, God willing, from Hellfire."
"12006","(12006) Zayd bin Harun told us, Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Sa’sa’ bin Mu'awiyah, he said: I met Abu Dharr and said: Tell me a hadith that I heard from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says: There are no Muslims for whom three of their children who have not yet reached puberty die due to perjury. Except that God will admit them to Paradise thanks to His mercy. (Nasa’i 2002. Ahmad 5/151)"
"12007","(12007) Zaid bin Harun told us, Al-Awwam bin Hawshab told us, he said: Abu Muhammad, the servant of Omar bin Al-Khattab, told me. On the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Both Muslims will go to Three of their children had not yet reached puberty, but God admitted them to Paradise. Abu Dharr said: Two of them left, O Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And two. Abu al-Mundhir, the master of the Qur’ans, said: One has passed, O Messenger of God. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And one, and that is in the first time. (Tirmidhi 1061, Ahmad 1/429)"
"12008","(12008) Shababah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh, on the authority of his father: That a man used to come to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and his son was with him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: Do you love him? He said: God loved you as I loved him. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, lost him and said: What did your son do? He said: Did you notice? He died, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Are you not pleased that you will not enter one of the gates of Paradise? You asked for it to be opened, but he came running and opened it for you. He said: O Messenger of God, is it for him in particular or for the people in general? He said: May you be rewarded. (Nasa’i 1997, Ahmad 3/436)"
"12009","(12009) Musaab bin Al-Miqdam told us, Mandal told us, Al-Hasan bin Al-Hakam told us, on the authority of Asma bint Abis, on the authority of her father On the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Indeed, a miscarriage will grieve with his Lord if He causes his parents to enter the Fire, until it is said Oh, the fallen one, who is detested by his Lord. Raise up, for I have admitted your parents to Paradise. He said: So let them drag them along with their secrets, until they enter them. Heaven (Ibn Majah 1608 and Bazzar 815)"
"12010","(12010) Khaled bin Mukhlid told us, Yazid bin Abdul Malik Al-Nawfali told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Roman, on the authority of Abu Harry, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A fallen man whom I present in front of me is more beloved to me than a knight whom I succeed in. Behind you (Ibn Majah 1607)"
"12011","(12011) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, who said: A woman narrated to me. She used to come to us and it was said to her: “She has a shelter.” She went to see Ubad Allah bin Muammar, and there was with him a man from the Prophet’s companions. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the man Ubaid Allah ibn Mu’mar narrated this: On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that a woman She brought him a boy of hers, and she said: O Messenger of God, pray that he may remain alive, for three days have passed, so he said: O Messenger of God, pray that he may remain alive. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Since she converted to Islam,” she said, “Yes.” He said, “A jinn protected from the Fire.” However, he said to her, “Since Three jinn, fortified from the Fire, converted to Islam. She said: Then `Ubaidullah said to me: O my refuge, come, so listen to this hadith. She said: So I heard it, then she left from Ubaid Allah and came to us and narrated it to us."
"12012","(12012) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the man and the woman are buried in a grave The man was presented in front of the woman."
"12013","(12013) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, and Ata’; Concerning the man and the woman being buried in the grave. They said: The man is presented before the woman in the grave."
"12014","(12014) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, that when Ali prayed over the funerals of men and women, he made The men are from those of their color and the women are from those next to it. And when he buries them, the man comes first and the women last."
"12015","(12015) Abd al-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders; Concerning a man and a woman being buried in one grave. He said: The man is presented before her."
"12016","(12016) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of his followers, who said: If a man and a woman are buried in one grave, he makes The man in front of the woman."
"12017","(12017) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, on the authority of Wathili bin Al-Asqa’; Concerning a Christian woman who had a child born to a Muslim in her womb. He said: She will be buried in a cemetery that is not a Jewish cemetery. And the Christians."
"12018","(12018) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, who said: A woman died in the Levant and in her womb was a child born to a Muslim man. She was a Christian, so Omar ordered that she be buried with the Muslims for the sake of her son."
"12019","(12019) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzali, on the authority of al-Qasim, who said: A menstruating woman should not pray at a funeral."
"12020","(12020) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhall, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: He was asked about a menstruating woman praying over a funeral procession. He said: No and no. The pure one"
"12021","(12021) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Habib bin Abi Thabit, who said: I asked Ata’ whether a menstruating woman should pray for him. The funeral? He said: No."
"12022","(12022) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, that Abu Ubaidah prayed over people in the Levant."
"12023","(12023) Issa told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khalid bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, a similar story."
"12024","(12024) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, that Abu Ayyub prayed over a man."
